update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (Fall 2025): the in-state / out-of-state / international / unknown rows add up to the totals (3,797 applied, 3,701 admitted, 1,225 enrolled). Only 7 first-year international applicants (6 admitted, 6 enrolled) appear in this Common Data Set, so the international admit rate is not meaningful. 3.00% (33 students) submitted SAT and 87.00% (1,067) submitted ACT. The SAT composite row (25th/50th/75th = 900/900/1160) looks like a data-entry slip (50th equals 25th), so the SAT total is not shown. The PDF uses an unreadable font encoding; numbers were read by page coordinates and cross-checked (GPA bands sum to 99.99%). The admission-factor checkboxes could not be read, so admission factors are not shown. Undergraduate enrollment is 8,279 (''Total Undergraduates''; 5,277 degree-seeking, the rest mostly non-degree/dual-credit); international undergraduates number 93 (the nonresident total).'
