update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'Figures from IPEDS, the US government''s college data (fall 2023 first-time, first-year class: 13,274 applicants, 12,851 admitted, 994 enrolled). College Navigator also shows fall 2024: 11,867 applicants, 97% admitted, 7% of admitted students enrolled (rounded percentages; no counts given). No public Common Data Set was found on csueastbay.edu (the Institutional Effectiveness & Research office publishes dashboards instead), so applications by residency (international applicants and admits), GPA and score ranges are not available. Undergraduate enrollment is the fall 2024 College Navigator figure (9,909); international undergraduate headcount is not published there (only 4% of first-time students came from foreign countries in fall 2023), so the number of international undergraduates is not shown. CSU campuses are test-blind, so there are no SAT/ACT percentiles.'
