update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set PDF''s fillable fields, fall 2024 first-year class: applicants 3,855 men + 5,063 women = 8,918, admitted 3,444 + 4,637 = 8,081, enrolled 759 + 860 = 1,619 (College Navigator shows 8,919 applicants, 91% admitted, 20% of admits enrolled). The residency table sums to only 8,442 applicants / 7,894 admits / 1,612 enrolled and does not fill in the international column, so no international applicant or admit counts are shown. The Common Data Set lists a further 1% with GPA below 1.0. CWU has no waitlist, no early decision or early action, and no application closing date; applicants are admitted until classes start (priority date 3/1, which differs from the Jan 31 on CWU''s admissions page). On open admission, the Common Data Set answered ''Other'': a 2.0 GPA with rare exceptions. The SAT/ACT ranges and the admission factors grid could not be read reliably from the 2024-25 Common Data Set, so scores and factors are not shown.'
