update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set, fall 2025 first-year class (residency table: 22,542 applicants, 20,528 admits, 2,041 enrolled; 7 applicants and 1 admit had unknown residency). International applicants numbered 239 and admits 150 (63%), a rate far lower than the overall admit rate of about 91%. Chico State has no waitlist and no early decision or early action. Undergraduate enrollment 13,599 and 145 nonresident undergraduates are the ''Total Undergraduates'' figures. The CSU is test-blind: only 3% (69) of enrolled first-years sent SAT scores and 0.5% (8) sent ACT scores, so score ranges are not shown. The admission factor ''standardized test scores'' is marked very important in the Common Data Set, which contradicts its test policy answer (SAT/ACT not used), so that single factor is left out.'
