update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2025): 24,549 applied, 17,192 admitted, 2,931 enrolled; residency by known address at application: in-state 6,101 applied / 4,341 admitted, out-of-state 18,225 / 12,757, international 223 applied / 94 admitted / 20 enrolled (international admit rate is well below the overall rate). Early decision: 348 applied, 303 admitted. The Common Data Set lists 29% of enrolled first-years submitting SAT and 10% ACT; Coastal runs a test-optional program for freshmen with a 3.5 HS GPA. The GPA breakdown is the ''all enrolled students'' column (sums to 99.99). The test score table is laid out unevenly in the PDF text; SAT section, SAT total and ACT composite percentiles were matched against the score-range distributions printed beside them. ACT subscore percentiles were not readable and are not shown. The admission-factor checkboxes are garbled (several rows show two marks), so factors are not shown.'
