update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2025): applicants = 5,886 men + 7,279 women; admits = 4,879 men + 6,067 women (the unknown-sex admit cell is suppressed, ''C or t'', and unknown-sex applicants are 0). CMU reports an open admission policy for all students (with selective admission to some programs). The in-state/out-of-state/international split of applicants and admits is suppressed in the Common Data Set, so no international admit rate can be shown; degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates were 101 (the total-undergraduate nonresident cell is suppressed). The GPA breakdown is only printed for the ''students who submitted scores'' column; the average GPA of 3.38 covers all who submitted a GPA. Undergraduate enrollment is the ''Total All Undergraduates'' figure (9,459).'
