update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set, fall 2024 first-year class: applicants = 15,130 men + 18,122 women + 98 another gender; admits = 13,821 + 16,929 + 92. Enrolled 5,543 is the full-time plus part-time total (2,578+34 men, 2,875+37 women, 19 another gender); the separate enrolled-by-gender lines add to a lower 4,655, an inconsistency in CSUN''s Common Data Set. CSUN did not report the residency breakdown (in-state, out-of-state, international), so no international admit rate can be shown; 125 first-time first-year students and 950 degree-seeking undergraduates were nonresidents. CSUN did not report SAT/ACT score ranges, and the admission-factor check boxes could not be read reliably, so scores and factors are not shown. CSU campuses are test-blind. College Navigator (IPEDS) shows 33,005 applicants and 93% admitted for fall 2024.'
