update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'The latest Common Data Set U of I posts is for fall 2023 (2023-24), so these figures are two classes old. Newer figures from IPEDS, the US government''s college data (fall 2024 entering class): 13,443 applied, 10,154 admitted (75.5%), 2,025 enrolled. The international row (2,208 applied, 753 admitted, 116 enrolled) counts all international applicants, so it likely includes many who were admitted but never completed or did not qualify; U of I says its minimum GPA for international first-year applicants is 2.5. Undergraduate counts are the Common Data Set ''Total Undergraduates'' (9,269, of whom 399 are nonresident) as of fall 2023; U of I''s newsroom reports fall 2025 undergraduate headcount of 7,978. Student-faculty ratio is fall 2023 (17 to 1). No early decision or early action.'
