update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (Fall 2025 first-time first-year, IU Indianapolis campus): 16,460 applied, 12,846 admitted (78%). International: 625 applied, 350 admitted (56%), 19 enrolled, so international applicants are admitted far less often than domestic ones. No early decision; no waitlist. 28.5% (918) of enrolled students sent SAT scores and 2.4% (78) sent ACT scores. IU Indianapolis was created in 2024 when IUPUI was split; every figure here is from the IU Indianapolis Fall 2025 Common Data Set, and no IUPUI-era figure is included. The admission-factor checkboxes could not be read reliably from the text, so they are left out. Undergraduate enrollment and the number of international undergraduates come from the ''Total Undergraduates'' figures (14,834; nonresident 273 including non-degree students).'
