update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2025 entering class; applicants = male 2,755 + female 5,196). International first-years: 113 applied, 111 admitted (98%), 8 enrolled, so IUP admitted almost every international applicant. Open to nearly all applicants (91% overall admit rate). SAT/ACT are optional. SAT percentiles are for the 25% (460) of enrolled first-years who sent scores; ACT figures come from only 11 students and are unreliable. The GPA breakdown is for all enrolled students. Undergraduate enrollment is 7,425 (total); there are 59 nonresident degree-seeking undergraduates (135 counting non-degree-seeking). The Common Data Set PDF text is jumbled in places; values were cross-checked by sums (residency totals match the applicant counts).'
