update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set, applicants by residency: 7,479 in-state, 14,011 out-of-state and 697 international. The international admit rate is calculated as 657/697 = 94.3%, with 157 enrolled. Undergraduate enrollment is 22,544 (all undergraduates), of whom 690 are international (nonresident aliens). No early decision or early action; no waitlist. Admission is formula-style: students are assured admission with a 3.25+ GPA, or ACT 21 / SAT 1060 with a 2.0+ GPA (per the Common Data Set); international applicants are admitted at a 2.5 GPA per the international admissions page.'
from public.institutions i
