update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2025). The college did not report the in-state/out-of-state/international split, so international applicant and admit counts are not available. No waitlist; no early decision or early action. Undergraduate enrollment is 46,069 (all undergraduates, including non-degree-seeking); international undergraduates number 901 (counted as nonresidents). SAT composite 25/50/75 = 1010/1100/1210 (mean 1111); only the ACT composite mean (22.4) is given, so ACT percentiles are not shown. Note: KSU now requires SAT/ACT and raises the minimum high school GPA to 3.0 for fall 2027 entry, so the 2025 admit rate (79%) overstates how easy fall 2027 admission will be.'
