update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2025): 7,460 applied, 6,231 admitted, 1,685 enrolled; applicants by residency: 7,260 in-state, 132 out-of-state and 68 international (60 admitted, 11 enrolled). Texas-based applicant pool: only 68 international applicants. The printed SAT composite row is inconsistent with the section scores, so no SAT total is shown; section and ACT percentiles come from the Common Data Set (45% of enrolled first-years sent SAT scores, 5% sent ACT scores). The GPA-range table is garbled in the PDF text, so no GPA breakdown is shown. No early decision or early action; admission is rolling with no closing date. International undergraduates (counted as nonresidents) number 82 (80 degree-seeking). The Common Data Set student-to-faculty line is outdated (fall 2022), so the ratio is from College Navigator (20 to 1).'
