update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'Fall 2025 first-year class (from the Common Data Set). International applicants were admitted at 49.8% (1,061 of 2,129) versus 63.6% overall, so international admission is tighter than the headline rate. Undergraduate enrollment is 18,444 and the nonresident count is 436 (total-undergraduate figures). Only 6.6% of enrollees submitted SAT (215 students) versus 91.8% ACT (2,999). The Common Data Set marks SAT/ACT ''required to be considered'' but the admissions site offers guaranteed admission on a 3.0 GPA alone; no early decision or early action; deferral up to one semester. The Common Data Set did not report the nonacademic admission factors.'
