update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set, fall 2025 first-year class: 19,136 applied (7,614 men + 11,453 women + 69 unknown sex), 15,908 admitted (83%), 3,747 enrolled (men 1,612, women 2,114, unknown sex 21, full-time plus part-time). The university did not report the residency breakdown (in-state, out-of-state, international), so no international admit rate can be shown. College Navigator (fall 2024) shows 17,679 applicants and 74% admitted. SAT/ACT percentiles cover the 16% (SAT, 593 students) and 61% (ACT, 2,284 students) of enrollees who submitted scores. The GPA table prints only two populated columns (students who submitted scores / did not) and a blank all-students column, so no GPA breakdown is shown. The admission-factor check boxes could not be read reliably, so factors are omitted.'
