update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2025): applicants 9,169 (3,306 men + 5,849 women + 14 unknown), admitted 8,196, enrolled 1,408; residency table: in-state 7,388/6,707, out-of-state 1,211/1,016, international 563/471 applied/admitted (18 international enrolled). The Common Data Set reports no waitlist. The GPA breakdown is the ''all enrolled students'' column as printed. Undergraduate enrollment is 6,206 (the ''Total All Undergraduates'' line). The share of students who sent ACT scores is printed as ''<1%'' (9 students) and shown as 1 percent. The admission factor checkboxes are unreadable as text, so the factors are omitted. The student-faculty ratio of 14:1 is from College Navigator (fall 2024); the Common Data Set does not print it.'
