update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'Figures from IPEDS, the US government''s college data (fall 2023 first-time degree-seeking entering class); no readable Common Data Set was found on saintleo.edu, so SAT/ACT, GPA, residency and international splits are not available (international applicants and admits are not shown). IPEDS does not separate University Campus (residential) first-years from online students; only 632 enrolled, so the cohort is mostly residential. College Navigator''s fall 2024 figures: 6,684 applicants, 78% admitted, 13% of admitted enrolled (admit counts not printed). Saint Leo is test-optional and reported no SAT/ACT submitters in IPEDS 2023. Undergraduate enrollment 7,516 (fall 2024) and the 25:1 student-faculty ratio are university-wide and include the large online/WorldWide population; Saint Leo says international students are over 22% of its University Campus undergraduates (about 600 students on campus), which is not in IPEDS.'
