update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set: international first-year applicants 228, admitted 81 (36%), enrolled 6, far below the 74% overall admit rate, so SRU is not an automatic admit for international applicants; the Common Data Set does not say why (for example incomplete applications). The waitlist section says there is no waitlist policy, while SRU''s admissions page describes a waitlist for applicants below the guidelines. 12% (178 students) of enrolled first-years submitted SAT; the Common Data Set prints ACT as 0% with 30 students, so the share of students who sent ACT scores is not shown. SAT/ACT percentiles are for those submitters only (ACT: 30 students). The admission factors section marks test scores ''important'' although applications are test-optional. The GPA breakdown is the all-enrolled column (3.58 average). Undergraduate enrollment 7,088 and 248 nonresident undergraduates are from the Common Data Set (fall 2025).'
