update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2023): applicants, admits and enrollees are the sums of the men/women/another-gender rows (4,785 / 3,817 / 504). The residency table shows 4,724 / 3,783 / 504 in total, with International 570 applied, 206 admitted, 17 enrolled (about 36% of international applicants admitted versus about 80% overall), In-state 2,197 / 1,911 / 322 and Out-of-state 1,957 / 1,666 / 165; the residency totals are slightly below the overall totals, so in-state and out-of-state counts are not shown. 21% (108) of enrolled first-years sent SAT scores and 52% (262) sent ACT scores. The GPA ranges are for all enrolled students; 1.5% of students were below 1.0. College Navigator for fall 2024 shows 5,949 applicants and about 80% admitted. Undergraduate enrollment is 2,666 and the nonresident count is 115 (the ''Total Undergraduates'' column, fall 2023); the admission-factor checkboxes could not be read from the PDF, so factors are not shown.'
