  and i.slug = 'uh-downtown';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'Figures from IPEDS, the US government''s college data (fall 2024 entering class); no Common Data Set was found for the university (the search result labelled as its Common Data Set belongs to the University of Houston-Downtown, and tamuv.edu has no Common Data Set page under institutional research), so test scores, GPA, residency and international applicant splits are not available. IPEDS shows 1,880 applicants, 1,803 admitted (96%) and 221 enrolled; College Navigator reports no SAT/ACT score percentiles. Undergraduate enrollment 2,627 and the 15-to-1 student-faculty ratio are from College Navigator (fall 2024). The school was named University of Houston-Victoria until 2025 and is now Texas A&M University-Victoria (IPEDS 225502).'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = '6e7d5ba7-134f-5866-a653-0202ec1fb200'
  and t.cds_year = '2024-2025'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'uh-victoria';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2025 entering class): 69 international first-year applicants, 65 admitted, 12 enrolled. The Common Data Set reports no waitlist; early action closing date is Dec. 1 with rolling notification. Percentiles are as printed for the 92 SAT and 13 ACT submitters; the workbook''s ACT sub-score rows look mis-aligned, so only the ACT composite is shown. Undergraduate enrollment 2,337 and nonresident undergraduates 77 are from the Common Data Set enrollment section (fall 2025).'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = '426b3118-c3d0-5bfd-94d8-255d0a711d1b'
  and t.cds_year = '2025-2026'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'uis';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'UIUC does not report GPA in the Common Data Set. The residency breakdown in the Common Data Set contains spreadsheet errors (#REF!) and is not shown. EA closes 11/1, notification 1/30; no ED. Application fee $50 domestic / $75 international.'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = '4bbd7e56-a2f5-5ab6-9af7-1e0b6c3abb6d'
  and t.cds_year = '2025-2026'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'uiuc';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'Figures from IPEDS, the US government''s college data (fall 2024), as shown on College Navigator: 4,224 applicants, 85% admitted (80% of men, 88% of women), 35% of those admitted enrolled. College Navigator prints rounded percentages, so the admit and enrolled counts are not shown. No ULM Common Data Set could be found (not listed on ulm.edu Academic Affairs data resources or in searches), so GPA, residency/international splits and admission factors are not shown. Score percentiles are for enrolled first-time students; 14% (165 students) sent SAT scores and 86% (1,040) sent ACT scores, so the SAT ranges rest on a small, self-selected group. Undergraduate enrollment is fall 2024 (6,761); the international undergraduate count is not published in the sources checked.'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = 'a1139982-6511-5fbf-a792-1cdacc8d9610'
  and t.cds_year = '2024-2025'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'ul-monroe';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2024); totals are men + women + unknown and match the residency total row. The residency breakdown (in-state / out-of-state / international) is internally inconsistent as printed (e.g. enrolled in-state 1,054 against 555 total enrolled), so international applicants and admits are not shown. The 2025-2026 Common Data Set was not found: the Institutional Analysis site blocks automated access and the newest Common Data Set on its page (Internet Archive copy, Aug 2025) is 2024-2025. Undergraduate enrollment is the total (5,011, includes part-time and non-degree students); the number of international undergraduates is the nonresident total (59). Student-to-faculty ratio 14:1. The ''Percent in top tenth/quarter'' class-rank entries look unreliable (based on 1 reporting student) and are not used. SAT/ACT percentiles are for enrolled first-time students who sent scores (64% sent SAT scores, 3% sent ACT scores).'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = '5936e534-1437-56ae-a762-ff38e77e1972'
  and t.cds_year = '2024-2025'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'um-flint';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'GPA figures come from the all-enrolled column of the Common Data Set. Only 24.9% of enrolled first-years sent SAT scores, so SAT/ACT ranges describe a small self-selected group. The share who sent ACT scores is not shown: the Common Data Set prints 0.3% beside a count of 160 (about 3.0%), which conflict. The average GPA is a weighted figure (above 4.0). Early action closes 11/5. Fall 2025 entering class.'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = '3e512b67-e6f8-5a28-ac52-6d439854761e'
  and t.cds_year = '2025-2026'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'umass-amherst';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2023 entering class). This is the newest Common Data Set UMass Boston had posted on its Common Data Set page when checked (2023-2024; no 2024-25 or 2025-26 file listed), so the figures are two cycles old. Residency split: in-state 12,558 / out-of-state 6,279 / international 2,081 applicants; 10,044 / 5,470 / 1,839 admitted; 1,968 / 287 / 208 enrolled. Undergraduate enrollment and the nonresident count are the ''Total Undergraduates'' figures (12,234; 844 international). The Common Data Set marks admission as open for most students with selective admission to some programs. SAT/ACT percentiles cover only the 28% (695) / 2% (54) of enrollees who sent scores; the GPA ''all enrolled'' column sums to 99%. Application dates in the Common Data Set (2023-24): priority date 11/1, closing date 2/15.'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = '1532a872-1f5b-5818-af57-e857d8bb7a85'
  and t.cds_year = '2023-2024'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'umass-boston';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set 2024-2025 (fall 2024 entering class): exact counts; the residency columns also include 3 applicants of unknown residency. International admit rate 687 of 761. Only 10% of enrollees sent SAT scores and 1% sent ACT scores, so the percentiles come from a small group. The GPA breakdown and the admission factor checkboxes could not be read automatically, so they are not shown. The 2025-2026 Common Data Set was not found as a file (the university''s archive page stops at 2024-25); this is the latest readable year.'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = '4b498114-f00f-50c8-b50f-e87a704ecf30'
  and t.cds_year = '2024-2025'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'umass-dartmouth';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (fall 2024 entering class); this is the newest one on UMass Lowell''s Common Data Set page when checked, so the figures are one cycle old. Residency split (known physical address): in-state 10,271 / out-of-state 2,783 / international 622 applicants; 8,503 / 2,296 / 546 admitted; 1,778 / 193 / 40 enrolled. Undergraduate enrollment is the ''Total undergraduate Students'' figure (6,897 + 5,211 + 3 + 11 = 12,122); the nonresident count (305) is the ''Total Undergraduates'' column. SAT/ACT percentiles cover only the 27% (550) / 2% (46) of enrollees who sent scores. Application dates in the Common Data Set (2024-25): priority date Nov. 5, closing date June 1.'
from public.institutions i
where t.institution_id = '62f8aac6-4b22-5a10-a8a1-7a936d20386e'
  and t.cds_year = '2024-2025'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'umass-lowell';
update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'The Common Data Set residency split reports only in-state and out-of-state; international applicants are included in the out-of-state figures (not broken out). No early decision; non-binding early action (Nov 1). GPA is on a weighted scale (average 4.41, 89% shown as 4.0), so it is not comparable to unweighted GPAs. Competitive admission to Limited Enrollment Programs (e.g. Computer Science, Engineering, Business) is reviewed separately.'
from public.institutions i
