update public.admission_stats t set notes = 'Fall 2025 entering class. International first-year applicants 1,640, admitted only 118 (7%), enrolled 56 (residency table), so WCU admits far fewer internationals than domestic applicants. The total enrolled is not shown: the Common Data Set reports 2,936 enrolled (residency table; men 1,272 + women 1,679), but the full-time/part-time split (1,895) and the test-submission counts imply a class near 1,900. WCU says it receives 9-10 applications per fall first-year space. The undergraduate total of 10,268 and the 223 nonresident-alien undergraduates are from the Common Data Set.'
