update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'APU 2026-27 estimate for a first-year living on campus: tuition (12-18 units) $45,980, university service fee $800, housing $6,490, dining plan $4,800 = $58,070 (books and other costs not included). For F-1/J-1 visas the International Services page says proof of funds must show $65,871 for undergraduates, pending new health insurance costs; APU says every admitted traditional undergraduate gets some academic scholarship based on GPA and test scores. 2027-28 table (first-years, per year, renewable up to four years): Trustees full tuition; Presidents $24,000 (GPA 4.25+); Provosts $23,000 (4.0-4.24); Deans $21,000 (3.5-3.99); Directors $19,000 (3.0-3.49); Mary Hill Award $15,000 (under 3.0). The scholarship page does not say whether international students are eligible; an undated APU article says international students not winning the other merit awards are considered for International Scholarship I and II and the APU Grant (amounts there are outdated and not recorded). International students are not eligible for U.S. federal aid.'
