update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year and all-undergraduate costs from the Common Data Set (2026-27): tuition 50,660; required fees 1,600; food and housing 11,770 (housing 5,890 + meals 5,880); books 500; residential transportation 1,080 is not included in other costs. Non-need-based aid from the college is available to nonresidents; 40 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received aid from the college, average 45,317 (total 1,812,685); to apply for this aid, the college asks them only for an International Student''s Certification of Finances; Bellarmine says 100% of incoming first-year students receive institutional gift aid; Scarlet Scholarships (tuition awards, priority date Feb 1) are based on the admission application with no separate application. The CDS shows 40 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid averaging $45,317, and international aid is non-need-based. Need-based grants require the FAFSA. Bellarmine Scholars/Fellows need a separate scholarship application by Dec 1.'
