update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International in-person 2026-27: tuition for 12-18 hours $10,080 per semester ($20,160 per year); residence hall and meal plan $5,760 per semester ($11,520 per year; varies by hall and plan). Page estimate $31,680 per year excludes course fees and books (books $37 per credit hour, opt-out possible). Required international student insurance $2,114 per year. 2024-25 College Navigator listing was $18,712 tuition and fees; The international tuition/aid page lists first-year academic merit awards of $4,000-$12,000 per year (Presidential $12,000, Trustee $10,000, Provost $8,000, Deans $6,000, Bethel Honor $4,000); a 3.0 cumulative GPA or ACT 20 (if submitted) is considered competitive. Hendrix Scholarship (full tuition/fees/room/meals or tuition/fees) needs 3.5 GPA or ACT 24/SAT 1190; its listed deadline was Dec. 1, 2025. Athletic and Renaissance (audition) scholarships also exist. Need-based aid for international students is not described. Awards cover fall and spring for up to ten semesters.'
