update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International page, undergraduate 2026-27: tuition $376.40/credit x 30 = $11,292; general activity fees $1,203; international student fee $400 ($200/semester); discipline fees about $472 (not split out); standard double room $4,338 plus standard meal plan $4,100; health insurance $1,422 (shown under other costs); books $1,000; total $24,227, excluding $2,000-$5,000 personal spending per semester. SD resident tuition $8,024 from the Tuition & Fees page; that page''s financial-aid cost of attendance for a nonresident living on campus is $29,356 (includes miscellaneous and transportation); F-1 students are eligible for the Global Ambassador Scholarship (competitive, international-only; free on-campus housing for up to eight semesters, estimated at about $14,000 over four years; chosen on essay, GPA, test scores and activities) and for Scholarships of Distinction (up to $4,000 per year based on unweighted GPA and/or ACT/SAT). International students are not eligible for federal aid.'
