update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Fall 2026 / spring 2027 full-time undergraduate (12+ credits) annual tuition: in-state $6,672, out-of-state $17,880. Annual mandatory fees (same for both): athletic $1,250, intramural and recreation $64, health service $191, university construction $218, student center $1,250, student activity $221, technology $309, plus sustainability $2.50 and Bulldog Card $13 per semester (total $3,534). The page does not state that international students pay the out-of-state rate, so international tuition is not shown. Housing runs about $3,936 to $6,854 per semester depending on hall, and meals $551 to $3,282 per semester, so housing and food is not shown. Bowie State did not report the cost section of its Common Data Set; No scholarship or aid page for international undergraduates was found, and the Common Data Set section on the college''s own aid for nonresidents is blank. The scholarships page lists private donor and departmental scholarships (nursing, computer science cybersecurity, education, band) open to new full-time students without saying whether F-1 students qualify. F-1 students are not eligible for the FAFSA (school code 002062 applies to U.S. aid applicants). Ask internationaloffice@bowiestate.edu or financial aid before relying on any award.'
from public.institutions i
