update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'On-Track campus semester tuition 2026-27 is $2,544 for Church members and $5,088 for non-members (international students who are not members pay the non-member rate). The yearly figures shown above cover two semesters: tuition is the member rate (5,088); international tuition is the non-member rate (10,176); housing and food is 2 x $2,898 (on-campus housing and food for a single student aged 18-25); books are 2 x $303. BYU-Idaho runs three semesters a year, so a three-semester year costs more. The school''s one-semester non-member cost of attendance for a single student aged 18-25 is $11,440 (tuition 5,088, loan fees 29, books 303, transportation 1,694, personal 1,428, housing and food 2,898). The international finances page (timestamped 2022, so possibly stale) asks for proof of funds of $23,750 a year for members and $29,000 for non-members and an initial deposit of at least $4,000 before the I-20 is issued; it lists a $6,000 foreign deposit for non-members in one table and about $4,000 elsewhere; The international finances page says there are no scholarships specific to international students; BYU-Idaho scholarships are open to anyone who meets their criteria. Four-year academic scholarships (full, half or quarter tuition: $2,544, $1,272 or $636 per semester in 2026-27) are applied automatically and need transcripts and ACT/SAT scores, but all BYU-Idaho scholarships are based on member tuition rates, so non-members receive less in dollar terms. Eligibility of international students and need-based aid for them is not stated.'
