update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the school''s non-resident estimate for students beginning Spring 2027 (15 units per semester): tuition and fees $24,496 combined (shown as international tuition; the page does not split fees out), health insurance $1,500 (shown under other costs), living expenses $18,509 (shown as housing and food), total I-20 amount $44,505. Dependents need $5,000 extra per spouse and per child; Global Scholarships (separate application in the Pioneer Scholarships Portal after submitting Cal State Apply): Global Excellence Scholarship is a limited number of full non-resident tuition waivers (over $14,000 per year), renewable up to four years, for freshmen with a 3.3+ GPA; Global Honors Scholarship is a limited number of one-year awards of $2,900+. Both ask applicants to demonstrate financial need and enroll in 15 units a semester; awards are competitive and not guaranteed. International students may apply only for merit-based awards in the general Pioneer Scholarships Portal (most $300 to $3,000). Conditional admission with the Global Academy Intensive English Program is available for students below the English minimum.'
