update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Computed from published rates: basic tuition $3,419 per semester (6.1+ units) twice, plus nonresident tuition of $471 per unit for an assumed 30 units a year ($14,130). Required fees = campus fees $547.04 per semester (Fall 2026 fee table: undergraduate total $3,966.04 minus tuition $3,419), doubled and rounded. Living costs are Cal State LA''s on-campus 2026-27 budget: housing $13,682 plus food $7,972; other = transportation $3,002 plus personal $4,726 plus loan fees $52. Total = the school''s $38,500 California-resident on-campus budget plus $14,130 nonresident tuition (its own tuition-and-fees line, $7,938, is $6 above the fee-table sum). International students must also carry health insurance; the cost was not found; In the Common Data Set, 8 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received the college''s own scholarship or grant aid (need-based or non-need-based, the Common Data Set does not say which), average $9,042, total $72,335. The Common Data Set tuition figures are not used; costs come from Cal State LA''s fee and cost-of-attendance pages; No international scholarship or admission-based merit award was found. Cal State LA''s scholarship FAQ (undated) says it has no special funds to recruit international students, though enrolled international students can compete for scholarships with other students after performing well. The Common Data Set does show 8 nonresident undergraduates received aid from the college itself, averaging $9,042. No conditional admission or English program is described on the pages checked. Confirm with the admissions office.'
