update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From CSUSB''s 2026-27 suggested international budget (undergraduate, 24 units): tuition and fees $20,359 combined, including the $471 per unit non-resident charge (shown as international tuition; the page does not split fees out); living expenses $19,786 (shown as housing and food), books and supplies $880, and other costs = transportation $2,906 plus health insurance $1,956 plus personal $4,414. Total $50,301. Dependents need $6,000 each per academic year; The Common Data Set reports no aid from the college itself awarded to degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates (0 recipients). The Common Data Set tuition figures are not used; costs come from CSUSB''s international tuition-and-fees page; The CSUSB catalog says scholarship aid for entering students is limited and none are specifically reserved for students from another country; no international merit scholarship or tuition waiver was found for undergraduates. The Common Data Set reports no recipients of the college''s own aid among degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates. Conditional admission is offered: students who are academically qualified but below the English minimum attend the CSUSB English Language Program (Level 3 for undergraduates, with an accelerated one-semester Level 3 option) before starting their degree; this needs two applications (one to the International Extension Program and one through Cal State Apply).'
