update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'CSUSM international estimate for 2026-27 at the 12-unit minimum load: tuition and fees $20,638 (basic tuition $6,838 + $471/unit non-resident charge for 24 units + fees $2,496, so the international tuition shown is 20,638 minus fees), room and board $19,245, living expenses $8,813 (mandatory 12-month health insurance, books and personal), total $48,696; summer not included. In-state tuition, out-of-state tuition (30 units) and required fees are Common Data Set values for 2026-27; The #YouAreWelcomeHere scholarship for first-year international applicants is advertised on the freshman page as covering up to 50% of non-resident tuition; the 2021 application form says a minimum of 50%, renewable up to 4 years with a 3.0 GPA, with a 500-1,000 word essay or short video and an April 1 deadline (confirm current terms with iapply@csusm.edu). Partial tuition waivers are only open to F-1 students after one semester in residence. International students are not eligible for most aid. Conditional admission: the Intensive English Pathway takes any English level, the University Access Program needs TOEFL 51 or IELTS 5.0; both lead to guaranteed admission (program fees not checked).'
from public.institutions i
