update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Estimated 2026-27 cost of attendance living on campus: tuition $41,250 (full-time, 12+ hours), fees $2,060, housing $8,280 and food $6,750 (shown together as housing and food), books $830, supplies $1,100, transportation $2,178, personal $5,642, course materials $586, federal loan fees $73; total $68,749. No separate international tuition rate is published; Merit scholarships (Scott-Ellis program) are determined automatically at admission for main-campus applicants, and the international page requires an SAT or ACT score sent by the testing agency ''for scholarship consideration''. No international-specific scholarship amounts are published; the FAQ gives an average aid package of $27,203 for all students. Federal aid does not apply to international students.'
