update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Campbellsville campus, traditional undergraduate living on campus: tuition $14,880 per semester (12-18 hours) x 2 = $29,760; technology fee $300 + activity fee $200; food and housing $10,984; books $800; total COA $48,362 including personal expenses, transportation and loan fees (published). The tuition page lists room and board of $4,884-$5,920 per semester depending on the hall. No separate international tuition rate is published; No international-specific scholarship was found. Freshman merit scholarships on the Campbellsville campus are set by high school GPA (Trustees up to $16,500, Provost up to $15,500, Dean up to $14,500, Founders up to $13,500 per year, renewable with a 2.0 GPA); a Presidential Scholarship (full tuition, housing and books) needs a 3.5 GPA or 25 ACT / 1200 SAT plus an essay and interview. The scholarships page does not say whether international students qualify, so eligibility is unconfirmed. International students cannot use FAFSA-based aid.'
