update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'CUA 2026-27 undergraduate estimated cost of attendance before aid: tuition $60,500 ($61,240 for Architecture and Engineering), fee allowance $1,774, housing $12,160 + food $8,780, books $1,286, and other $4,986 (transportation $1,068 + personal $2,634 + estimated loan fees $1,284), total $89,486. International applicants must document funds for the first year plus health insurance (the university enrolls students in its plan unless comparable coverage is shown); The international admission page says international students are eligible for Catholic University merit scholarships of up to $33,000 per year; awards are decided during the admission review (no separate application) from the high school record, not test scores, and 95% of first-years got CUA aid over the last 3 years (tuition page). The first-year scholarship page lists a Catholic University Scholarship of $17,000-$32,000 over four years (page undated), Archdiocesan and service scholarships, and departmental awards. Whether international students can receive need-based aid is not stated: the aid pages describe FAFSA-based need aid.'
