update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Tuition rates and fees are from the Common Data Set for 2026-27; the CCSU tuition page lists the international full-time rate as $13,455 per term (tuition and fees together); From the Common Data Set (2026-27): tuition in-state $6,998, out-of-state (New England/NEBHE rate) $10,498, nonresident $20,938; required fees $6,052; on-campus food and housing $13,472. The admissions-site tuition page lists an international full-time rate of $13,455 per term ($26,910 a year, tuition plus fees), within $80 of the Common Data Set nonresident tuition plus fees. Other costs = transportation $672 plus other expenses $1,589 (estimated expenses for residents). Only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 115 nonresident undergraduates received it, averaging $9,918; The college''s own aid for nonresidents is non-need-based only (Common Data Set: 115 nonresident undergraduates received it, average $9,918). CCSU awards merit scholarships to select newly admitted first-year students with no separate application; no international-specific scholarship names or amounts are published on the pages reviewed. The Honors Program carries a $4,500-per-year scholarship.'
from public.institutions i
