update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'CMU''s international undergraduate estimate for 2026-27 (24 credits, on-campus housing with a meal plan): tuition and fees $22,050, living expenses $17,596, health insurance $1,600; total $41,246. First-years must live on campus for two years; From the Common Data Set, first-year 2026-27: resident and non-resident US students pay the same $15,570; the international rate is $27,000 (before merit awards). Only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 27 nonresident undergraduates received it in 2024-25 (avg $16,805). The Common Data Set file is named ''cds-2024-2025'' but its cover and sections are the 2025-2026 edition; Automatic merit awards by GPA, no separate application: International President''s Award (3.3+ GPA) gives the U.S. resident tuition rate (about $9,144 per year saved); International Scholar Award (3.0-3.29) $4,000 per year for 4 years; International Opportunity Award (2.8-2.9) $1,000 per year for 4 years. Proof of English is required; government-sponsored students are not eligible. CMU says 34% of eligible international freshmen do not pay the full international rate. The competitive Centralis scholarship can cover tuition, fees and housing.'
from public.institutions i
