update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International tuition page (undated, accessed 2026-10-26; labeled 2026-2027 as the current page): undergraduate tuition and fees $19,900 per year at 12 credit hours per semester, housing and dining $10,300 (nine months), books, insurance and miscellaneous $2,260 (shown as other costs), total $32,460; College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $8,818, out-of-state $19,704; on-campus food and housing $9,700, other $8,400; the total cost of attendance is the out-of-state on-campus total; Applying for admission also applies for automatic freshman scholarships: Distinguished Global Scholar up to $16,000 over four years ($4,000/yr) for GPA 3.50 or SAT 1300 or ACT 28; Merit Global Scholar up to $12,000 ($3,000/yr) for GPA 3.25 or SAT 1250 or ACT 26; Honor Global Scholar up to $8,000 ($2,000/yr) for GPA 3.00 or SAT 1200 or ACT 24. Renewable with a 3.00-3.25 GPA. Extra funding (up to $4,500/yr total) for residents of Nigeria, Ghana, Malaysia, Vietnam, Thailand or Ivory Coast. UCO says it awards about $700,000 a year to international students.'
