update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Estimated 2026-27 cost of attendance for a freshman living on campus: tuition $34,270 (flat $17,135 per term for 12-18 hours), fees $800, housing $10,426 and food $3,548 (shown together as housing and food), transportation $1,190, personal $2,020; total $52,254. Books are not itemized. No separate international tuition rate is published. Enrollment deposit for international students is $100 (non-refundable); All international undergraduates are eligible for an automatic award at admission with no extra application: an International Student Scholarship of $10,000-$12,000 per year for students who attended schools outside the U.S., or an academic merit scholarship of $5,000-$19,000 per year (by GPA) for students from U.S. schools or international schools with a U.S. curriculum. The Global Ambassador full-tuition award is separate. The pages do not say whether need-based aid is open to international students; FAFSA-based aid is not.'
