update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Chico State''s estimated 2026-27 budget for an international undergraduate (9-month year): tuition and fees $9,288 plus nonresident tuition $11,304 (12 units x $471 x 2) = $20,592 (international tuition is tuition and required fees combined); housing $6,750 and meals $5,662 (housing and food together $12,412); books $1,122; personal $1,800 and health insurance $1,500 (other costs together $3,300); total $37,426. The page calls these estimates. The Common Data Set for 2025-26 listed tuition $6,450, nonresident tuition $19,552, required fees $2,446 and food and housing $16,668; International Student Excellence Scholarship (new first-year or transfer undergraduates on F-1): nonresident tuition fee waivers of $2,000 to $11,000, one year and not renewable; needs GPA 3.3+ and demonstrated financial need; number of awards not guaranteed; the page may be outdated. Wildcat Scholarships (over 700 awards, open to all students) are open January to mid-February. International students are not eligible for University Basic Needs grants.'
