update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'The Common Data Set lists 2024-25 costs (2025-26 costs were not final when it was filed); there is no separate international tuition, so nonresident tuition applies. 56% of full-time undergraduates pay more because tuition varies by program. 295 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid (avg $15,607); the Common Data Set checks both need-based and non-need-based aid as available to nonresidents; All admitted international undergraduates are automatically considered for scholarships of $2,000-$12,000 per year, renewable up to four years with good academic standing; no separate application. CSU says no institutional scholarship covers the full cost of attendance. Federal aid is limited to U.S. citizens and permanent residents. The Common Data Set checks both need-based and non-need-based institutional aid for nonresidents, but the aid pages do not describe need-based aid for international students, so need-based aid for international students is not yet confirmed.'
