update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set (it says final 2026-27 costs were due about Aug 1, 2026). Out-of-state and international tuition are the same ($20,846). The Common Data Set says institutional need-based aid is available to nonresidents (31 received it, avg $10,413) and non-need-based aid is marked ''No'', but the university''s scholarship page lists GPA-based merit scholarships for international students (see the aid note that follows); Scholarship page: GPA-based merit scholarships for international first-years who apply and pay the deposit by May 1; the page says award amounts will be finalized once the institutional aid budget is approved, so no amounts are given here. The Common Data Set instead marks need-based (not non-need-based) institutional aid for nonresidents, with 31 recipients averaging $10,413. International students are not eligible for federal aid.'
