update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Concordia''s 2026-27 undergraduate price list (not specific to international students): tuition $43,000, student services fee $800, basic housing $5,250 plus meal plan $6,700 (entered as $11,950), student accident insurance $160 (entered as other), total $55,910. The page says full-time students received on average $29,000 in scholarships and grants in 2024-25 (all students, not international only); international students also need their own health insurance; Academic merit scholarships are automatic on acceptance and the international acceptance packet includes the academic scholarship. Fall 2027 first-year amounts by high school GPA: Achievement Award $16,000 (2.00-3.37), Dean''s $17,000-$18,000 (3.38-3.87), Regent''s $19,000-$20,000 (3.88-4.0), President''s $24,000 (4.0 with ACT 31+). Faith-based awards (Lutheran Commitment minimum $29,000) require Lutheran membership or ties. Need-based grants are tied to the FAFSA, which international students cannot file.'
