update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Davenport''s 2026-27 undergraduate budget (30 credits, 8 months, dependent on-campus column): tuition and fees $32,945 combined, food and housing $14,280, books and supplies $780, personal $3,008 (transportation $944 and loan fees $66 are not included in other), total $52,023. Per-credit tuition is $1,059 on the first rate listed and $1,148 on a second block that names the Great Lakes Bay, Lansing and Warren campuses; the Grand Rapids rate was not confirmed. Tuition is the same for international students on the pages read; College Navigator 2024-25 (superseded by the 2026-27 figures in the cycle file): tuition and required fees $24,466; on-campus room and board $12,928; other expenses $3,280; The international page says merit-based scholarships of up to $10,000 per year may be available. The scholarships page lists Executive $10,000/yr (3.85+ GPA), Distinction $9,000 (3.50-3.84), Momentum $7,000 (3.0-3.49), Impact $6,000 (2.75-2.99) and Signature $5,000 (below 2.75); it does not say these are specific to international students, and it lists no international-only awards. Federal and state aid are not available to international students.'
