update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2026-27 full-time on-campus cost of attendance for business, humanities, health professions and science: tuition $34,276, housing and food $11,502, books $1,468, transportation $1,190, personal $3,146, loan fees $72 = $51,654. Architecture and engineering tuition is $35,498 (total $52,876). No separate international tuition rate is published; First-year costs for 2025-26 from the Common Data Set: tuition $33,606, required fees $0, food and housing $10,636 (commuter food and housing $11,280 is also printed); books and supplies $1,468. Tuition varies by program (15% of full-time undergraduates pay more). In the Common Data Set (2024-25 estimated), 126 degree-seeking undergraduate nonresidents received institutional aid, average $18,443 (total $2,323,779); International freshmen who enroll full-time (and pass the English requirement) receive a Detroit Mercy scholarship of up to $10,000 per academic year based on cumulative high school GPA; it is renewable and cannot be combined with other university grants. Canadian freshmen can also earn a $1,000 Visit Grant. International students are not eligible for federal or state aid. In the Common Data Set (2024-25 est.), 126 degree-seeking undergraduate nonresidents received institutional aid averaging $18,443, which is above the published $10,000 scholarship cap, so other awards may exist; the aid page describes no need-based aid for international undergraduates.'
