update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs for 2024-25 from the Common Data Set: in-state tuition $4,452, out-of-state/nonresident $20,729, required fees $2,909, on-campus housing $6,498 + food $4,852 = $11,350; books $1,510. The Common Data Set shows 2025-26 costs were not yet final. 53 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid (average $19,182, total $1,016,624); the Common Data Set text does not show whether it was need- or non-need-based. The tuition shown is the in-state figure; No international-specific scholarship, amount or need-based program is published on the pages read. Merit scholarships are applied for through the ECUAWard portal after admission (freshman deadline Dec 15, 2026 for eligibility); some also consider FAFSA need, which F-1 students cannot file. In the Common Data Set, 53 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $19,182.'
