update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'ETSU international estimated cost of attendance 2026-27 (undergraduate, 15 credit hours per semester): tuition and fees $30,686 (fees included, not split out), housing $5,000, board $4,320, textbooks and supplies $1,300, health insurance $1,614 and miscellaneous $5,240 (other = $6,854), total $48,160. The international cost-and-scholarships page shows a lower illustrative total of $40,006 (tuition $15,343 plus housing and meal plan $4,660 per semester, before insurance and miscellaneous); International Merit Scholarships need no separate application; every new degree-seeking international applicant is considered: Blue $5,000/year (high school GPA above 3.0), Gold $7,000/year (above 3.5), Elite $9,000/year (above 3.75), renewable for up to 8 semesters with a 2.75 GPA and full-time enrollment. They cannot be combined with scholarships that cover out-of-state tuition (e.g. Creative Arts or STEM Community Outreach, which reduce tuition to the in-state rate, roughly $19,000-$20,000 a year). ETSU reports more than $6,000,000 in institutional scholarships to international students in 2024-25. International students are not eligible for federal aid.'
