update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'EKU cost-of-attendance table, 2026-27 full-time on-campus: in-state tuition $5,325 per semester, ''Out of State & International'' $6,120 per semester (12-15 credit hours). Required fees per semester: $150 special use, $150 asset preservation, $255 Exceptional Eastern Experience (x2 = $1,110); a student health fee may also apply. Housing and food estimates on that table were ambiguous, so the housing and food figure comes from the 2024-25 College Navigator instead. Proof of funds required for the I-20: $28,614; College Navigator 2024-25 (tuition and fees, first-year full-time): in-state $10,320, out-of-state $21,230; on-campus food and housing $12,268; other expenses $3,650; No scholarship for new international undergraduates was found on EKU''s international page, and no CDS was readable for nonresident aid data. EKU''s merit scholarship tables are based on GPA and ACT and international eligibility is not stated; ask the admissions office (admissions@eku.edu).'
