update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the 2026-27 Tuition & Fees page (effective fall 2026 and spring 2027). Tuition $20,280 per semester x2 = $40,560 (12-18 credits). Student services fee $373 per semester x2 = $746. Room and board uses basic housing ($3,866 per semester) plus the board plan ($3,497 per semester) x2 = $14,726; other room types run up to $4,883 per semester (apartment) and a single-room premium of $775 per semester applies; From the Common Data Set: books and supplies $1,351 (2025-26). First-year tuition for 2025-26 was $39,188, required fees $928, on-campus food and housing $14,038; International Student Grant of $15,000-$26,000 for qualified international students (cannot be combined with other Eastern aid); on-campus employment averages about $1,000 per year; Church Matching Grant and Ministerial Discount may apply. First-year merit awards of $16,000-$27,000 are described for all admitted first-years, but the pages do not say whether they apply to international students. The scholarships page says undocumented and international students who want need-based institutional aid must file a paper FAFSA with tax returns and a letter; whether such aid is awarded to internationals is not stated. International students are not eligible for federal aid. The 2024-25 CDS nonresident aid figures could not be read reliably, so none are recorded.'
