update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Full-time undergraduate tuition $45,258 (2026-27), student fee $300 per term, room $7,454 plus 17-meal board $5,716.30; first-year students also pay a $275 matriculation fee. The cost-of-attendance page lists different room ($8,150) and food ($7,880) estimates, so budgets can differ from billed charges; Tuition, student fee ($300 per term) and room/board from Elmhurst''s 2026-27 tuition page (room $7,454 + 17-meal board $5,716.30, rounded); books from its cost-of-attendance page. New full-time first-year students also pay a one-time $275 matriculation fee. Private university: no separate international tuition; International first-year awards need no separate application and are based on the admission application: International Chairman''s Award up to $20,000 and International Discovery Award $1,000-$5,000 (academic merit), plus international student tuition grants (amounts not listed). The overview page says merit awards can be worth up to $20,000 per year. International students are not eligible for federal aid.'
