update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'ESU international page (no academic year is printed; entered as 2026-2027 as the current page): non-resident undergraduate flat-rate tuition and fees $15,675 (12+ credit hours with at least one on campus), on-campus living $9,950, insurance/books/etc. $3,000 (entered as other), total $28,625. The page also lists a lower ''Partnership/Diversity Award'' rate (tuition and fees $10,125, total $23,075) without stating who qualifies. Kansas resident total is $20,305; Presidential Scholarship is automatic from the admission application and transcripts: $1,250-$3,000 per year by unweighted GPA (3.0 to 3.95+) or ACT (21 to 30+), renewable with a 3.0 ESU GPA and 24 credit hours. The international page says it is based on SAT and/or GPA. Also an International Ambassador Scholarship (leadership) and transfer scholarships (24+ credits). Stackable scholarships cannot exceed the cost of attendance. No international need-based aid is described.'
