update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'NC Promise (starts fall 2027, international students eligible, no extra application): out-of-state undergraduate tuition $4,000 per semester, so $8,000 for two semesters. Fees $1,726, health insurance $1,312 and a traditional-dorm room and board estimate of $3,500 are printed per semester (the figures here are doubled for two semesters; health insurance, $2,624 for the year, is not included). The page''s per-semester total for out-of-state students living on campus is $10,538 (2027-2028 rates); College Navigator 2024-25: tuition includes required fees; total is the on-campus cost of attendance for North Carolina residents ($22,958 at the out-of-state rate). See the cycle file for the NC Promise rates starting fall 2027; The international page lists no institutional international scholarships; it points to a Scholarship Opportunities page for external funding for admitted international students. FSU merit scholarships for first-time freshmen (Platinum $5,000, Gold $3,000, Silver $2,000 per year for unweighted GPA 3.75+, 3.50-3.74, 3.2-3.49) need no extra application, but the pages do not say whether international students qualify. International students are eligible for the NC Promise tuition rate.'
