update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International page: estimated first-year international tuition $24,416 per year (14 credits per semester at $872 per credit; the page does not state the academic year). Housing, meal plan and health insurance about $15,336 per year. From the Common Data Set (2026-27, final July 2026): on-campus food and housing $12,035 for first-year students. Canadian students pay in-state tuition (about $14,952); Woodbridge N. Ferris Scholarships are automatic for first-time international students, based on high school GPA (4.0 scale) plus a submitted test score: Founder''s up to $10,000/yr (3.9 GPA and ACT 31/SAT 1350/TOEFL 96/IELTS 7.5/PTE 66/Duolingo 120), President''s $6,500 (4.0), Provost''s $5,500 (3.5), Dean''s $4,500 (3.25-3.49), Ferris Crimson $3,000 (3.0), each renewable at 2.75-3.3 cumulative GPA. The international page says awards of $3,000 to $10,000 are made at admission. Students can earn up to $15,000 a year in an on-campus job. From the Common Data Set: 68 nonresident undergraduates received aid from the college itself, averaging $12,130. No need-based aid for international students is described.'
