update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2026-27 undergraduate on-campus estimate (standard program, before aid): tuition $40,698, mandatory fees $1,500, housing $7,120 plus food $6,620, books and supplies $1,000, miscellaneous personal $1,544, transportation $1,030 (not included in other costs). The page shows no total, so the total cost of attendance is not shown. Pharmacy, Equestrian and Animal Science programs have different rates; College Navigator 2024-25 (superseded by the 2026-27 figures in the cycle file): tuition and fees $41,164; on-campus room and board $11,200; books $2,000; other $2,504; International undergraduate merit scholarships (2026-27) are applied automatically at admission with no separate application: Trustee $25,000 (GPA 4.0+, ACT 27/SAT 1290), Presidential $24,000 (3.9; 24/1190), Deans $22,500 (3.65; 21/1090), Faculty $20,000 (3.3), Merit $18,500 (3.29 or lower); a 30 ACT or 1360 SAT adds $2,000, and the highest applicable amount is used. Renewal terms are not stated. IELP students receive $750 per semester. No international need-based aid is described.'
