update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the 2026-27 fee sheet, full-time undergraduate per semester: tuition $5,192 for SC residents and $10,384 for non-residents, plus required fees (registration $20, activity $156, IT $112, facility $100 = $388); annual figures here are two semesters. Resident example total on the sheet: $5,580 per semester. Housing and dining: residence hall double room including the All-Access Plus meal plan is $5,685 per semester ($11,370 a year); apartments and other meal plans cost less or more. The sheet text is garbled in places; the non-resident tuition and housing figures were matched to the sheet''s own structure (non-resident total = $10,772 per semester, which equals College Navigator''s $21,544 annual tuition and fees for 2024-25). Books and other expenses not stated; The international page says international undergraduates pay all expenses and the University does not award financial aid to them, although some scholarships are available for qualified students. The Academic Distinction Award ($1,000+ for top 40% of class, SAT 1100/ACT 22, 3.0 GPA) is for South Carolina residents. The Admissions Scholarships application (due March 15) covers out-of-state waivers and other admissions scholarships ($500 up to full tuition, room and board); strong GPA (3.0 weighted), class rank and test scores are considered, and eligibility for international students is not spelled out. Students from Brandenburg, Thuringia, Rhineland-Palatinate (Germany), Queensland (Australia) and Taiwan may qualify for in-state tuition under the Sister-State initiative.'
from public.institutions i
