update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Fresno State''s estimate for Fall 2027/Spring 2028 (undergraduate, 12 units a semester): tuition and fees $20,979 (one combined figure), food and housing $11,634, books and insurance $2,978 (other), total $35,591. The Fall 2026/Spring 2027 estimate is $34,434. International students must buy the university-approved insurance; Dean''s Scholarship Tuition Waiver for international students and out-of-state residents, about $1,250 to $3,750 each (70+ international students received one last year). Muhareb Family Grant: $1,000 to $1,500 for a select group of newly admitted international students in their first semester, chosen on academic achievement, financial need and funding; no application, but send an expression of interest by May 15, 2027 (fall 2027). Conditional admission: students without a qualifying TOEFL/IELTS can be admitted to ESL plus a degree program (two-year language-study I-20, American English Institute on campus); placement needs one score report with no minimum. Same fall deadlines (July 1 outside the U.S., Aug 1 in the U.S.).'
