update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'College Navigator estimated expenses for full-time beginning undergraduates, 2024-25: tuition and fees $14,220 in-state / $38,688 out-of-state; on-campus food and housing $15,725; books $1,288; other $3,667; total on-campus $34,900 in-state / $59,368 out-of-state. 2026-27 rates were not checked; Mason offers a limited number of merit-based scholarships to highly qualified international freshmen and transfers on F-1 visas; all admitted applicants are considered automatically (no separate application) through a holistic review in which GPA and test scores matter most. Awards renew for up to four years for freshmen. Amounts are not published. Non-US citizens are not eligible for federal aid; the page does not describe need-based institutional aid for international students.'
