update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International estimate (tuition and fees 30,892 for 7+ credits per semester; room and meals 12,732; books 2,000; health insurance 2,998; other 1,106; total 49,728). In-state and domestic out-of-state figures not entered because a single clear 2025-26 page was not found; International Student Scholarships (ISS) are a full or one-half waiver of out-of-state tuition, based on academic ability, extracurricular involvement and financial need; apply with the ISS section of the international application, and a limited number are competed for once a year after enrollment. A Distinguished Scholars Award covering the out-of-state tuition difference (about $20,326 per year for fall 2026) is advertised to non-Georgia residents with a 3.64 high school GPA, SAT 1179 or ACT 25; the page does not say whether international students qualify. The dollar value of an ISS waiver is not published separately.'
