update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Tuition page (Fall 2026 to Summer 2027), flat rate for 15+ credits per semester, doubled for two semesters: in-state $2,070, out-of-state $8,280, out-of-country $8,520 per semester. Mandatory fees are the sum of the listed per-semester fees ($622) doubled; the cost-of-attendance page shows tuition plus mandatory fees of $17,814 for out-of-state residents (it is not specific to out-of-country tuition). Housing and meals $15,810 (on campus), books $1,670, miscellaneous $3,080; transportation $2,880 is not included in other costs. Total cost of attendance for out-of-country students is not published; F-1 students can apply to International Student and Scholar Services for an international out-of-state tuition waiver: limited, highly competitive, not guaranteed, judged on demonstrated financial need, essay quality and community service. The amount of the waiver is not published. Test scores may be required for other scholarships; no international merit scholarship is described.'
