update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International page ''Annual Cost Estimate for Undergraduate Students (2026-2027)'': tuition and fees $18,550 (12 credit hours), room and board $11,904, health insurance $2,936, personal expenses (books, supplies, transportation, entertainment) $4,200, total $37,590 (the page labels the total ''2024-2025'' by mistake). An I-20 requires proof of funds for at least one year of expenses; International Merit Scholarship (out-of-country tuition waiver) is worth about $13,000 per year, lasts 4 years for freshmen, is competitive, for fall admits only, priority deadline Feb. 1; criteria are good academic standing, financial need and commitment to the university. The page also says Georgia Southern offers a limited number of need-based and academic scholarships for international students. Freshman academic scholarships (Jan. 15) look for SAT 1300+ / ACT 28.'
