update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Non-resident table, 2026-27 header: matriculation $10,200 plus fees = $10,732 per semester (15 credits), so $21,464 per year. Housing and meals use the Oaks double room ($2,608) plus the Unlimited meal plan ($2,230) per semester, doubled; other halls cost more. Health insurance and personal expenses are not included. International students can seek a limited out-of-state tuition waiver worth about $13,000 (see aid); GSW says it has no scholarships specifically for international students. A limited number of out-of-state tuition waivers (about $13,000 savings) are offered, with priority to students completing the ELI with the Advanced Completion Certificate; the Outstanding Out-of-State Student waiver and Beginning Freshmen Scholarships (Feb. 1) are open to international applicants who send SAT or ACT scores.'
