update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Tuition page 2026-27: lower division (0-54 credits) Michigan resident $16,520/year, non-resident $23,492/year (12-15 credits per semester). Housing and food $11,100 (unlimited meal plan, traditional living center). Required fees are not itemized on that page. Books and other expenses are CDS G5 figures (not updated for 2026-27). Admitted international students on listed visa types receive the GVSU International Scholarship, so they pay the Michigan rate; First-year costs from the Common Data Set; the Common Data Set notes that final 2026-27 charges were not yet available, so the figures from the college''s tuition page are shown instead. 222 nonresident degree-seeking undergraduates received aid from the college itself, average $9,304; GVSU International Scholarship: automatic for admitted undergraduate international students on E2, F1, H4, K2, L2, R2, TN or TD visas; covers the non-resident surcharge so they pay the Michigan tuition rate (about $6,700 per year, renewable up to 4 years). International Merit Scholarship: $2,500 per year, renewable up to four years, for fall-start first-time college students with a separate application (recommended by Feb 15). The two can be combined.'
