update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year estimate for 30 credit hours on Harding''s cost page (the page does not label its year, so 2026-27 is assumed): tuition $945 per hour = $28,350, technology fee $1,200, freshman housing $5,000, all-access meals $5,400 = $39,950 billable. The international admissions page still shows an older estimate ($37,484 including a $500 international fee and $1,692 health insurance with tuition $25,590), so budget extra for the international fee and mandatory insurance; Federal aid is not available to international students and the university will not give assistance above actual tuition. Admitted freshmen can receive an Academic Achievement Scholarship of $7,000-$11,000 per year for four years based on test scores and GPA (full-time, 3.0 GPA to renew); the Trustee Scholar full-tuition award needs a 3.5 GPA and ACT 31 / SAT 1390 / CLT 100. The pages do not say whether these awards are open to international students. The College of Business lists a Sam Walton Scholarship ($3,000 per year, preference to non-U.S. business majors).'
