update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UH Hilo 2026-27 international budget as on the I-20: tuition $20,448, estimated fees $770, meals and housing $10,814, books and supplies $1,350, and other $5,876 (transportation $1,500 + personal care $2,776 + required medical insurance $1,600), total $39,258. The page''s summary line for books and medical insurance ($2,935) does not match its itemized $2,950, so the itemized figures are used; UH Hilo International Student Scholarship: a limited number are awarded each year to F-1 students with outstanding academic merit and financial need; admitted new international students are considered automatically (no separate application) and notified by email. No amounts are published. International students can also use the UH System Common Scholarship Application (the 2026-27 deadline was March 2; 2027-28 dates not yet posted) and college dean''s scholarships. International students on F-1 visas do not file the FAFSA.'
from public.institutions i
