update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (2025-26, first-year): it lists one nonresident tuition figure ($22,646) equal to out-of-state tuition, shown here as international tuition. The university tuition page lists 2026-27 out-of-state/international tuition of $11,641 per semester (about $23,282 per year; in-state $4,989 per semester unchanged); An International Scholar Award of $5,000 a year (renewable up to three more years, first-year international students not fully sponsored, 3.0 high school GPA, automatic consideration when admitted by the deadline) appears in a university scholarship listing, but that listing is not dated for fall 2027 (its status reads ''Ended on 03/01/2021'') and the current page could not be reached, so confirm with scholarships@indstate.edu. The freshman scholarships page says many awards give first consideration to students admitted by Dec. 1 and does not mention international status. The aid-policy checkboxes in the Common Data Set are not legible. International students are not eligible for federal aid.'
from public.institutions i
