update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Estimated 2026-27 costs from the Admissions cost pages (Iowa did not report costs in its Common Data Set). The tuition figures are tuition and fees combined: Iowa residents $11,971, nonresidents $34,247, international Liberal Arts & Sciences $35,442 (Business $38,847, Engineering $37,030, Nursing $39,316). The total of $53,042 is the international Liberal Arts & Sciences estimate and includes $2,628 health insurance. Common Data Set aid figures (final 2024-25): only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 161 degree-seeking nonresidents received aid, averaging $23,085 ($3,716,639 total); National Scholars Award for nonresident first-years (includes international): $2,000-$15,000 per year for up to four years, awarded automatically on admission to those with a complete application by Feb. 1, 2027, based on GPA and test scores (scholarship reviewed both with and without a score; test scores at or above 26 ACT/1230 SAT open larger awards). Renewal needs a 2.75 GPA and full-time enrollment. International students do not qualify for need-based aid from Student Financial Aid.'
