update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year rates from the Common Data Set (it ticks ''2026-27 costs not available yet'', so these are assumed to be 2025-26 rates; the ''Nonresident'' tuition line is shown as international tuition). Aid (final 2024-25): only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 566 degree-seeking nonresidents received aid from the college itself, averaging $13,144 ($7,439,681 total). Tuition varies by program (63% pay more than the first-year figure); Automatic International Student Excellence Award for admitted first-years, no separate application: President''s $56,000 total ($14,000/yr, needs SAT/ACT), Dean''s $48,000 ($12,000/yr, needs SAT/ACT), Innovator''s $40,000 ($10,000/yr, GPA 3.70+, no test needed), Launchpad $24,000 ($6,000/yr, GPA 3.50-3.69, no test needed); up to 8 semesters. Cannot be combined with the competitive International Merit Scholarship (OneApp; up to $40,000 or $16,000). Must accept the offer by May 1.'
