update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Providence catalog 2026-27 (estimated, subject to change): annual tuition $45,408; student activity fee $250; New International Student Services Fee $1,386 per year (the $476 new student fee does not apply to international students). Room only ranges $7,000-$16,000 depending on residence hall and occupancy; the Gold meal plan ($7,360) is required for new residential students (other plans $600-$6,212). Student health insurance $2,670. Room and board total, books and other costs are not given as a single figure, so they are not shown. ESL program students pay $5,250 tuition per semester and are not eligible for JWU scholarships or grants; The International Presidential Scholarship is awarded to incoming international students who show academic excellence; amounts vary (no figures published), renewable up to four years of full-time day study, and eligibility is decided during the admission review. Need-based JWU grants noted in the catalog exclude international students; whether any need-based aid exists for international students is not stated. Students in the ESL program are not eligible for JWU scholarships or grants. Visit scholarships (up to $5,000 for fall 2026 if visiting by Dec. 31) are open to domestic and international first-years.'
from public.institutions i
