update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (2025-26): out-of-state tuition is also paid by international students. Aid (final AY2025): only the college''s own non-need-based aid (International Admissions Scholarships); 330 international undergraduates received aid, averaging $12,572 ($4,148,695 total). The international admissions cost page (year not printed) estimates $33,854 tuition and fees plus $18,424 living expenses = $52,278 per year. Course fees vary by school; Renewable freshman scholarships based on high school GPA alone, available to international students (up to $64,000 over a KU career): KU Excellence 3.95-4.00 GPA $16,000/yr; Distinction 3.85-3.94 $14,000/yr; Achievement 3.70-3.84 $12,000/yr; Performance 3.50-3.69 $10,000/yr; Access 3.25-3.49 $8,000/yr. Renewal needs a 3.0 KU GPA and full-time enrollment; first bachelor''s degree or eight semesters. Apply for admission by May 1 to be considered.'
