update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27): in-state tuition $12,714; out-of-state/non-resident tuition $34,383 (international students pay the non-resident rate); required fees $1,463; housing $11,700 + food $5,348; books $1,200; other expenses $3,240 and transportation $2,592-$2,756 (not included in other costs); International freshmen admitted for fall are considered for the renewable Bluegrass Scholarship ($6,500 at 3.0 GPA; $10,000 at 3.5 or 3.0 with SAT 1200; $13,000 at 3.6 or 3.5 with SAT 1200; $16,000 at 3.8 or 3.5 with SAT 1360; deadline Dec. 1), the William C. Parker Scholarship (variable amount, holistic review of all applicants with GPA 3.0+, priority Dec. 1) and the International Ambassador Scholarship (listed as $3,000, min GPA 2.5, priority Feb. 15). Scholarships can be combined; none are awarded for spring. Need-based aid for internationals is not mentioned.'
from public.institutions i
