update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2026-27 academic year from the LC State international cost page and Certificate of Financial Responsibility: tuition and fees $23,938 (Idaho resident portion $8,226 plus a non-resident/international portion of $15,712), shared dorm room and meal plan $8,687, other (health insurance, course materials) $2,150; $34,775 is the total shown on the I-20. Costs are subject to change; New undergraduates are automatically considered for the Presidential Academic Waiver: with a 3.0+ GPA it is $6,115 per semester, applied only to the non-resident portion of tuition. It renews each semester with a 3.0 cumulative GPA and 12+ credits, and is not available to fully sponsor-funded students. Other scholarships and waivers are listed by the Financial Aid Office. Bridge students are not eligible during their Bridge terms. Whether need-based aid exists for international students is not stated.'
from public.institutions i
