update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International page and the 2026-2027 Financial Certification Form: tuition and fees combined $29,180, room $9,300 plus meal plan $5,270 = $14,570, subtotal $43,750 (the minimum annual support to show; excludes books, transportation, health insurance). Longwood''s cost page estimates $22,140 per semester for out-of-state students including room and the default meal plan (banded 12-18 credits); The international page lists merit scholarships for freshman applicants with a 3.0+ GPA (priority for applying by Dec 1), renewable for four years with a 3.0 GPA and 30 credits a year, plus Cormier Honors College scholarships (two full rides) and NCAA Division I athletic scholarships. Fall 2027 amounts on the financial aid page, Early Action (by Dec 1, 2026) / later: Presidential (4.0+) up to $7,000 / $6,000; Provost (3.75-3.99) up to $6,000 / $5,000; Dean''s (3.50-3.74) up to $5,000 / $4,000; Rotunda (3.25-3.49) up to $3,000 / $2,000; Lancer Distinction (3.0-3.24) up to $2,000 / $1,000 per year. That page does not name international students, but the international page links to the same awards. Need-based aid for international students is not described.'
