update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year figures from the Common Data Set. The international admissions page gives its own nine-month budget: tuition and fees $23,418 ($12,369 with the Bulldog Out-of-State Scholarship), living expenses $5,370, books and insurance $1,900, total $30,688 ($19,639 with the scholarship); no year is printed on that page. The Common Data Set says non-need-based aid from the college is available to nonresidents but gives no counts or amounts; The Bulldog Out-of-State Scholarship is an out-of-state tuition waiver worth about 50% of tuition costs (the international page''s example: tuition and fees $23,418 vs $12,369); recipients count as in-state for tuition. International freshmen need a 2.5 US-scale GPA, one admission test (TOEFL 4.5/79, IELTS 6.5, Duolingo 105, PTE 58, SAT 1130 or ACT 23), one English criterion (test, SAT English 500, ACT 23, Accuplacer 250) and one math criterion (SAT Math 510, Accuplacer 250 or a 3.0 GPA); keep a 2.0 quarterly GPA. Accept it in the application portal and upload the signed agreement. International students get no need-based aid.'
