update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27): tuition $56,930, required fees $1,580, food and housing $17,980 (housing $11,270 + food $6,710). Private university with one tuition rate. The college''s own need-based and non-need-based aid are both available to nonresidents; 229 degree-seeking nonresidents received it, average $26,906 (total $6,161,586); International applicants are automatically considered for merit scholarships when they apply; the award is in the acceptance letter. The Financial Aid Office lists academic scholarships of $14,000 to $34,000 per year for students entering fall 2026, while the admissions page says $20,000 to $34,000; the range for fall 2027 entrants is not published. Special scholarships needing separate applications (portal, early January) run from $2,500 to full tuition. International students cannot get federal aid. From the Common Data Set: the college''s own need-based and non-need-based aid are available to nonresidents; 229 received it, average $26,906.'
from public.institutions i
