update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Full-time undergraduate (12-18 credits): tuition $21,339 per semester; fees per year: technology $550, student activity $250, health & well-being $200, facility $400. Excludes nursing fee ($2,300 per year), health insurance, and a one-time $450 new first-college freshman fee. Room and board is not on the tuition page (the 2023-24 Common Data Set lists $17,000 for 2024-25). The average award is the 2023-24 Common Data Set average of the college''s own awards to 133 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates ($18,534); The international page says eligible full-time first-year applicants are automatically offered the highest scholarship they qualify for with their admission application. The general first-year merit list (not specific to international students) runs from Presidential, up to $28,000 a year with on-campus housing and up to $20,000 for commuters, down to Achievement Award, up to $20,000 / $16,000; renewable for four years with a 2.0 GPA. Need-based aid for international students is not described, so it is left unconfirmed.'
