update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Metro State charges the same tuition rate to all students regardless of residency ($322.00 per undergraduate credit plus $42.30 per credit in standard course fees). The $10,930 is the university''s own estimate for 15 credits per term over two terms. Cost of attendance page (2026-27): tuition and fees $10,930, books $1,500, living allowance $15,864, personal expenses $5,246, transportation $3,818, total $37,357. Other = personal + transportation. There is no campus housing, so the living figure is an allowance only. Nursing BSN and natural sciences courses carry extra per-credit differentials; No international-specific scholarship or aid was found on the international pages or the grants and scholarships page. The federal and state grants listed there are applied for through the FAFSA, and the Minnesota State Grant is for Minnesota residents.'
from public.institutions i
