update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'MTSU financial-aid cost of attendance for 2026-27 (14 credits): out-of-state tuition and fees $34,888 vs in-state $11,424, books $1,260, on-campus living $13,460, misc $2,314 and transportation $3,168 (other = $5,482), total $55,090 out-of-state on campus. MTSU pages do not list a separate international rate, so the out-of-state rate is the relevant one for F-1 students. Mandatory international health insurance $1,729 per year unless covered privately. From the Common Data Set: 296 nonresident undergraduates received the college''s own non-need aid, average $15,064 (the Common Data Set did not report tuition and fees); F-1 first-year and transfer students are considered for renewable international merit scholarships: Global Scholar $16,000/year (GPA 3.75-4.0, SAT 1370+ or ACT 30+), International Achievement $12,000 (GPA 3.5-3.74 or SAT 1210+/ACT 25+), International Access $6,000 (GPA 3.0-3.49, SAT 1040+/ACT 20+). Priority deadlines June 1 (fall) and Oct 1 (spring); funds run out first-come, first-served. Contact: international@mtsu.edu. The Common Data Set marks only the college''s own non-need-based aid for nonresidents.'
