update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'MSU cost-of-attendance page, 2026-27: tuition and fees combined $10,732 (Texas resident) and $23,570 (U.S. non-resident); the international table repeats the non-resident figures. Total $40,358 is the non-resident on/off-campus total (housing and meals $11,814, books $1,000, transportation $1,600, personal $2,374); the international table prints books as $140, which does not add up to its total. College Navigator listed 2024-25 out-of-state tuition and fees of $12,530, far below the current $23,570, so confirm with MSU; The international students page lists Academic Merit, Donor, Global Ambassadors, Good Neighbor, International Baccalaureate and Mexican Border Nation Waiver scholarships but prints no amounts, eligibility or deadlines (amounts ''vary every new academic year''). Academic merit scholarships for freshmen require SAT/ACT scores. Also accepted on the test-score page: iTEP 4.0, which has no separate field here.'
