update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27): in-state tuition $9,405, out-of-state and international $18,810, required fees $900, room and board $9,032.40. The Common Data Set also shows that 99 nonresident undergraduates received non-need-based institutional aid, average $7,899. MSSU''s 2026-27 international guide adds a $100 international student fee, $250 one-time orientation fee and $2,526.36 health insurance and book rental, for a year total of $31,618.76 (30 credits, double room, 19 meals). The international fee shown is that $100 fee; MOSO International Achievement Scholarship $5,500 for the first year (24 credit hours) for freshmen educated outside the US with 2.75 high school GPA and the English minimums (renewable up to 8 semesters with 2.75 college GPA); MOSO First-Year International Award $1,000 one-time (2.25 GPA); MOSO International Retention Scholarship $1,000 ($500 per semester) after 24 credits with 3.0 GPA. From the Common Data Set: 99 nonresidents received non-need-based aid, average $7,899. No international need-based aid found.'
