update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International Costs page (undated, accessed 2026-10-26; labeled 2026-2027 as the current page): undergraduate tuition and fees $23,760 per year at 15 credit hours per semester, living expenses $15,068 (housing, food and personal, not itemised, shown as other costs), health insurance $1,691, total $40,519. Before the 40% I Succeed reduction; College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $9,502, out-of-state $18,770; on-campus food and housing $11,006, other $3,924; the total cost of attendance shown is the out-of-state on-campus total; Missouri State publishes a 40% reduction in international tuition (the International Partnership Scholarship) for students who complete the 14-credit ''I Succeed'' first-semester package, which is required for students at CEFR B1 English and optional at B2+; the page says the lower price continues for all classes (about $3,475 saved per semester, exact prices may change). No other international merit scholarship or need-based aid was found, so the aid policy is left unset.'
