update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Bursar schedule for fall 2026 to spring 2027, full-time (12+ credits) undergraduate, doubled to a year: Maryland resident tuition $2,967.50/semester, non-resident $8,632.50/semester, fees $1,265.50/semester. The page does not state that international students pay the non-resident rate, so international tuition is not shown. Mandatory health insurance is separate ($781.95 fall + $1,159.05 spring = $1,941.00). Room and board are not given as annual totals, so they are not shown; Morgan''s freshman scholarship page lists the Troy E. Quinn Merit Award (up to $6,000 per year, automatic for first-time full-time fall freshmen; apply by Dec 1) and the J.C. Bozeman Need Grant (up to $2,000, non-Maryland residents, requires FAFSA, so not available to international students). The page does not say whether international students qualify for any award and its eligibility text refers to fall 2020, so confirm with Financial Aid (finaid@morgan.edu).'
