update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International costs page, bachelor''s degree, one academic year: tuition and fees combined $15,990, housing and meals $12,484, books and insurance $2,232, total $30,706 (this is also the bank-balance requirement). The page does not print the academic year; its transfer scholarship table is labelled 2026-27; Common Data Set 2025-2026: only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 642 undergraduate nonresidents received it (average $10,874, total $6,980,824). Murray State did not report tuition in the Common Data Set, so tuition and costs come from Murray State''s international costs page; From the Common Data Set: only the college''s own non-need-based aid for nonresidents. The first-year Academic Achievement scholarships ($1,000-$10,000, by GPA) and the Presidential Fellowship are domestic-only. International students can compete for general competitive scholarships after admission, and first-time transfer students get $1,500-$5,000 a year by GPA (2.75+). No published international freshman award schedule was found; ask msu.intl@murraystate.edu.'
