update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International base-rate undergraduate tuition AND fees estimate for 2 semesters of 12 credits ($753.32 tuition + $71.70 fees per credit); engineering $21,862. The cost page does not label the academic year. Housing $4,885 (shared) + 7-day meal plan $5,762 = $10,647. Also listed: ISS support fee $250, health insurance $2,190, one-time $200 new student fee. Page total $34,287 (base rate). Domestic tuition not checked; Automatic international scholarship by U.S.-equivalent GPA, up to 8 semesters: 3.5-4.0 = $12,000 ($1,500/semester); 3.0-3.49 = $8,000 ($1,000/semester). NDSU states it offers no full scholarships. Applicants may also be considered for conditional admission. From the Common Data Set (2024-25): only the college''s own non-need-based aid for nonresidents; 53 received it, average $8,382.'
