update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year rates for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set; the ''Non-resident (International)'' tuition line is the one shown. Aid (final 2024-25): 120 degree-seeking nonresidents received institutional aid, averaging $10,391 ($1,246,965 total); the web edition does not show which aid types are ticked. Tuition varies by program (43% pay more than the listed tuition figure); All admitted international students are automatically reviewed for Global tuition scholarships (holistic, no separate application; must meet the English requirement for unconditional admission, pay the enrollment deposit by May 1 and have all materials in by then): Global Laureate $15,000/yr (up to $60,000), Global Ambassador $10,000/yr (up to $40,000), Global Delegate $4,000/yr (up to $16,000), for up to four years with a 3.0 GPA and 24 credits per year. The need-based status of aid for nonresidents is not confirmed from the sources reviewed.'
