update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UNK Global costs page (2026-27, 15 credit hours a semester, double room, meal plan): international tuition and fees $18,193, housing and meal plan $12,294, health insurance $4,577, total $35,064 before the tuition waiver ($30,267 after the $4,797 waiver); books and indirect costs are not included. The international fee shown is the required health insurance. The Common Data Set lists required fees of $2,153 for first-year students, $50 less than implied by the $18,193 page total; First-year figures from the Common Data Set: in-state tuition $7,320, nonresident tuition $15,990 ($533 x 30 credits), required fees $2,153, food and housing $12,294; books $798. The Common Data Set box says 2026-27 costs were not yet final when it was completed, so the in-state tuition, fees and books may be 2025-26 values; the nonresident rate and housing match the UNK 2026-27 international cost page. In the Common Data Set, only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 63 nonresident undergraduates received it (average $4,301); All admitted international degree-seeking students on campus are automatically considered for the International Loper Tuition Waiver: a 30% cut in nonresident tuition (from $533 to $373.10 per credit hour in 2026-27), about $4,797 per year and $19,188 over four years, for 12+ credit hours a semester, renewable with a 2.5 GPA and 24+ hours a year, up to ten semesters. The scholarship page also prints older figures ($4,599/yr and $18,396 over four years, and a heading of $4,383); the 2026-27 rate table and the costs page both use $4,797. The Kearney Noon Rotary International Scholarship also exists but lists no amount. Federal aid is not available to international students. From the Common Data Set: 63 nonresidents received non-need-based aid from the college (average $4,301).'
