update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UNO estimate for fall 2026 / spring 2027, full-time on campus: tuition and fees $9,880 Nebraska resident, $26,400 out-of-state; housing and food $13,548; books $1,264; personal $2,540 plus transportation $1,700 (shown as other costs). The total cost of attendance shown is the out-of-state on-campus total. The page does not state an international rate; international students are not Nebraska residents and the out-of-state figure is shown as the closest published rate. Some colleges (Engineering, Business, IS&T) carry extra tuition per the checklist; College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $8,718, out-of-state $23,206; on-campus food and housing $12,130, other $4,032; the total cost of attendance shown is the out-of-state on-campus total; International Academic Excellence Scholarship funds partial tuition starting at about $3,000 per year (actual amount varies with tuition), renewable up to five years, for on-campus full-time study; all newly admitted first-time and transfer undergraduates are considered automatically after admission. Smaller awards: Sieu Mei Tu Endowment (graduates of Asian high schools, amount varies, fall deadline April 1) and Tom and Janet Miller ($1,000, IEP alumni with financial hardship).'
