update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UNR international undergraduate cost table (the page does not state an academic year; shown as the current estimate): base tuition $9,383 ($312.75/credit, 30 credits) plus non-resident tuition fee $20,189 (international tuition 29,572), mandatory student fees $1,841 (incl. international student fees). On-campus housing $7,000-$11,000 and meals $5,928-$7,488; the housing and food figure and the total both use the low end (published total range $45,541-$51,101). The 2025-26 Common Data Set lists nonresident tuition $28,308 plus fees $1,642. Health insurance and personal costs are not in the total. A separate admissions page still says $23,562 a year in estimated tuition, which conflicts with the cost table; The international admissions page says new international students can receive $1,000 to $12,000 scholarships, and general University scholarships range from $500 to $8,000 per year. OISS awards $300-$5,000 per year to degree-seeking F-1/J-1 students. Need-based help for international students is limited to the Institutional Methodology form after one year of study (priority Feb. 1). A Pack Exchange Program (200% of base tuition) exists only for international students who graduated from a U.S. high school in listed western states. From the Common Data Set (2025-26): 1,484 nonresident undergraduates received the college''s own aid, average $2,862. No conditional-admission or intensive-English pathway is described on the pages checked.'
