update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2026-27 estimate, full-time resident on campus: tuition $49,340 plus general fee $1,930 = $51,270; food and housing $20,998 (weighted average); books $1,324; indirect other $2,638 (miscellaneous $2,026, transportation $544, loan fees $68); total $76,230. International students also pay mandatory health insurance of $1,900 (shown as the international fee), which is not in the total. The page lists no separate international tuition rate; College Navigator 2024-25 for full-time beginning undergraduates living on campus; tuition includes required fees. Current 2026-27 figures are in the cycle file; The financial aid office does not award aid to international students (FAFSA-based). All first-time applicants are automatically considered for merit scholarships of $15,000-$33,000 per year, applied to tuition, renewable up to eight semesters; the page does not separate international students. Early Decision and Early Action admits get a minimum $20,000 per year. International students pay mandatory student health insurance ($1,900 in 2026-27).'
