update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'College Navigator 2024-25: published tuition and fees $9,172 in-state / $14,008 out-of-state (fees included); on-campus room and board $11,292; books and supplies $1,300; total on-campus cost of attendance $26,204 in-state / $31,040 out-of-state (the out-of-state figure is the total cost of attendance shown). The bursar page also lists a $150 ''International Fee'' and a non-resident fee for students who are not Louisiana residents; the university''s I-20 estimate is about $35,000 per academic year plus $5,000 per dependent (see the other notes); Awards for first-time, full-time international undergraduates (no FAFSA needed): International Tuition Award up to $2,000 per aid year and up to $8,000 over 4 years (3.0 non-weighted cumulative GPA, priority deadline Dec. 15) and International Book Award up to $1,000 (2.5 GPA, one-year limit, priority Dec. 15). Institutional scholarships go only to students entering in fall or summer. The larger freshman scholarships (Homer Hitt $75,000, President $20,000, Provost $16,000 and others over 4 years) are listed under domestic undergraduates, and the page does not state whether international students can receive them. The bursar page''s yearly estimates (15 hours per semester, year not labeled) are $10,518 for Louisiana residents and $15,354 for non-residents, plus a $150 international fee.'
