update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Nicholls'' cost-of-attendance page shows only 2025-2026 estimates (no 2026-27 figures yet), for a resident full-time undergraduate living on campus: tuition and mandatory fees $8,672 (combined), food and housing $11,248, books $1,385, transportation $3,650, personal $2,666, loan fees $72 (other costs = 3,650 + 2,666 + 72), total $27,693. The international page states international students do not pay out-of-state fees, so the resident figure is shown as the international tuition; No international-specific scholarship was found. Freshman academic scholarships are set by GPA and ACT (for example $2,000-$3,000 per year for a 3.0-3.5 GPA with ACT 21-30+; ACT-based, superscore not used), and the international page says an approved scholarship can offset the financial-support requirement, but eligibility of international students is not stated. International students pay the same tuition as Louisiana residents (no out-of-state fee).'
