update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $8,183, out-of-state $25,307; on-campus food and housing $12,282, other $4,536; the total cost of attendance shown is the out-of-state on-campus total. NMSU''s International Competitive Scholarship can reduce an international student''s tuition to the in-state rate (see aid notes); International Competitive Scholarship: a tuition discount (in-state instead of out-of-state tuition) plus a $100 cash stipend each fall and spring, for new degree-seeking F-1 students with an I-20, renewable up to 8 semesters. Freshman eligibility e.g. GPA 3.50 with TOEFL 68 / IELTS 6.0 / Duolingo 95, or GPA 3.25 with TOEFL 79 / IELTS 6.5 / Duolingo 100, or GPA 3.50 for students from English-exempt countries. Awards are limited and competitive and the separate application closes when awards run out. (TOEFL values here are the scholarship tiers, not the admission minimum.)'
