update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International office estimate for 30 undergraduate credit hours over nine months: tuition and fees $26,547 + living expenses $8,280 + books, supplies and technology $1,700 = $36,527. The page prints no academic year. Academic English Program (20 courses) is estimated at $24,477; From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27): in-state tuition $10,500 ($350 per credit hour x 30), nonresident $21,000 ($700 per credit hour), required fees $3,200, on-campus food and housing $11,050. The Common Data Set also shows that 338 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received the college''s own aid (average $14,021, total $4,739,086); both the need-based and non-need-based aid boxes are ticked; International recruitment scholarship: $10,000 for the first year ($5,000 per semester) for all admitted undergraduates who study on campus; the FAQ gives a range of $8,000-$10,000 per year. Keep a 2.5+ GPA after semester 3 to keep the full amount. The Global Learning Community scholarship adds $1,500 per semester applied to eligible UNA housing. No separate scholarship application or essay; UNA says it offers no fully-funded scholarships and states that 95% of international students receive scholarships. The Common Data Set also ticks need-based aid from the college for nonresidents, but the international office describes only these automatic scholarships.'
