update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27): in-state $5,730, out-of-state $21,150, nonresident $21,780, required fees $1,180, housing $7,164 + food $4,844. A Common Data Set box is checked to say final 2026-27 costs were not yet available (expected June), so the figures may be provisional; check the tuition estimator. Per credit hour: $191 in-state. Transportation estimate $1,340 not included. Admissions says international applicants must prove about $43,000 (bachelor''s) in funds and pay a one-time $200 international student fee on the Dahlonega campus; USG requires billed international student health insurance; International students do not qualify for US financial aid. After academic admission they receive information about the International Student Scholarship, which reduces tuition by roughly $3,000 per semester (approximate figure from the admissions FAQ). The Common Data Set marks both need-based and non-need aid from the college as available to nonresidents but gives no counts or amounts.'
