update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (2026-27): nonresident tuition equals out-of-state tuition ($29,568); housing and food = housing $7,790 + food $6,642; other costs = other expenses $2,000 + transportation $2,500. 20% of full-time undergraduates pay more because of program fees. Only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 129 received it (avg $9,320); International Excellence Award (IEA): up to $11,000 per year as an out-of-state tuition waiver for first-time, full-time F-1 undergraduates on the Flagstaff campus with a 3.0+ GPA at admission; no separate application, awarded first come, first served; renewable with full-time enrollment and a 3.0 GPA. Not available to sponsored students or dual-degree or PIE students. The Common Data Set says nonresidents get institutional non-need-based aid only. Foreign citizens are not eligible for FAFSA.'
