update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International page, undergraduate, Aug 2026-May 2027: tuition $21,578, fees $1,451, mandatory health insurance $2,520, books $500, housing and meals $10,646, personal $1,500, total $38,196. College of Business majors pay about $2,058 more as juniors/seniors; First-year costs from the Common Data Set (2026-27); tuition varies by program for about 12.8% of undergraduates. In the Common Data Set, 68 nonresident undergraduates received the college''s own non-need-based aid, average $5,771; there is no need-based aid for nonresidents; Automatic International Scholars Award of $2,000-$5,000 per year (renewable up to four years) for a 3.0 GPA or SAT 1020+, no separate application. International Excel Award $1,000-$4,000 per year (needs proof of English, leadership/service examples and the UNI Scholarship Application); Presidential Scholar Award $4,000 per year (3.80+ GPA and ACT 29+/SAT 1340+, or 3.95+ GPA test-optional). Partner-state students (e.g. Taiwan, Hebei, Maharashtra) get an extra $4,000 award. The Common Data Set shows 68 nonresident undergraduates received non-need institutional aid, average $5,771.'
