update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'NKU international costs page, standard rate: $625 per credit hour, $7,500 per semester (12+ credits); fees $850 (vary by program); residence hall $7,360 + meal plan $4,954 (typical); books $900; required health insurance $1,786; estimate $30,850. A lower $463/credit rate applies only to F-1 students graduating from Kentucky, Ohio or Indiana high schools. 2026-27 rates not yet posted; In the 2023-2024 Common Data Set, 298 undergraduate degree-seeking nonresidents received institutional aid, average $15,100 (total $4,499,790); the Common Data Set does not say whether it was need- or non-need-based. The tuition entries in the Common Data Set were not readable; tuition and fees come from NKU''s international costs page; NKU''s international admission and cost pages publish no scholarship amounts for new international freshmen; the international-student scholarship page only lists awards for current NKU students (e.g. Weiss $500). The 2023-2024 Common Data Set shows 298 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid (average $15,100), so institutional aid exists but the program is not published; ask isss@nku.edu.'
