update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2026-27 yearly estimates for 30 credit hours: tuition and fees combined $10,077 resident (includes new freshmen from the listed South Dakota Advantage states) and $12,379 out-of-state; housing $6,300 (average residence hall) plus food $4,974 (21 meals/week) = $11,274. The page does not say which rate international students pay, though the factsheet (titled 2023/2024) lists a $200 per-semester international student fee and ~$1,316 health insurance on top of tuition; current amounts are not confirmed. Out-of-state per-credit tuition is $376.40; The WolfPACT merit scholarship (4-year totals from $4,000 for a 3.00-3.49 GPA with no/low test score, up to $16,000 for a 3.75+ GPA with ACT 28+/SAT 1300+; 3.0 GPA to renew) needs no separate application. The current WolfPACT page says ''all first-year students'' without naming international students; the factsheet (titled 2023/2024) says WolfPACT is available to international degree-seekers and points to patrick.woods@northern.edu for other awards. Whether international students can receive need-based aid is not stated on the pages read.'
