update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Long Island campus, living in a dorm, 2026-27: tuition $48,300 (B.S./D.O. and B.Arch. $52,300), college fees $2,600, housing $24,000, food $7,024, books $1,620, miscellaneous $2,640, transportation $3,262, loan fees $72 (total $89,518; New York City campus dorm total $83,564). International undergraduates must document $77,650 ($81,650 for architecture majors) for the first year to receive an I-20; International students are not eligible for federal or state aid. First-year international students are automatically reviewed for tuition-only academic scholarships at admission (no separate application, no test scores needed), renewable for up to eight semesters with a minimum GPA. 2026-27 international first-year awards by GPA / high school average: $32,000 (4.0+ / 100+), $31,000 (3.75-3.99 / 95-99.99), $29,000 (3.5-3.74 / 90-94.99), $27,500 (3.20-3.49 / 84-89.99), $23,500 (3.0-3.19 / 80-83.99). The page does not say whether any institutional need-based aid exists for international students.'
