update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International page estimate (fall and winter, 12-14 credits per semester): out-of-state tuition $19,788, living expenses $11,454 (entered under room and board), medical insurance $2,292 (under other), total $33,534; budget about $4,000 more for books and personal costs. $15,426 is the in-state-equivalent tuition shown for Canadian/Mexican students with the Non-Resident Award. The page does not date this table. 2026-27 per-credit rates: non-resident lower division $795.75 (upper $853.25); Michigan lower division $574.50. OU charges no mandatory fees; First-year costs from the Common Data Set (labelled 2025-2026); the figures from Oakland''s international page replace these. Only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 127 nonresident undergraduates received it (average $5,851); OU''s scholarship page says international students are not eligible for OU scholarships except where noted; the Non-Resident Award (in-state tuition rate) goes to U.S. out-of-state students and to citizens and permanent residents of Canada and Mexico with a 2.5+ GPA, who must live on campus two years. The international viewbook nevertheless says competitive scholarships for international students exist and the Common Data Set shows 127 nonresidents received institutional non-need-based aid (average $5,851), but no international award amounts are published.'
