update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'OHIO''s international Athens estimate for one academic year (2026-27): tuition and fees $26,792 (not split), lodging (Classic Double) $8,954 plus meals (Traditional 14) $5,582, personal expenses $2,259 and health insurance $3,239 (other = $5,498); total $46,826. A separate books figure is not listed. The OHIO Guarantee fixes tuition, room, meal plan and fees for four years for nonresident students; College Navigator estimated expenses for full-time beginning undergraduates, 2024-25 (tuition and required fees; on-campus food and housing). The international 2026-27 estimate is on the admissions cost page; International first-years admitted directly to an academic program (not English/pathway programs) are considered for merit awards when starting in fall; merit is based on recalculated 4.0 GPA, test scores are used only if they raise eligibility, and the early-action application (Nov. 15) is the scholarship application. Amounts are not published for international students (the OHIO Trustee Award for nonresidents is up to $7,000 per year, but the page does not say whether international students are eligible). No need-based aid policy for international students is described.'
