update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs from the Common Data Set (2025-26): tuition is 30 credit hours at $180.55 resident / $697.90 nonresident per credit hour ($5,416.50 / $20,937.00); housing and food is the on-campus figure. The transportation estimate of $2,300 is not included in other costs. The college''s own need-based and non-need-based aid are both available to nonresidents; 169 nonresident undergraduates received it (avg $10,492); International Achievement Freshmen Scholarships (automatic with the application, partial tuition waiver) range $5,000-$15,000 per year; the grid is by GPA and test (e.g. IELTS 6.0 / SAT 1160-1220 with 3.0-3.24 GPA = $9,500; ''GPA only, no test'' awards $6,000-$9,000). Alumni legacy $5,000. College/department scholarships vary. The Common Data Set says need-based aid is also available to nonresidents (169 recipients, avg $10,492). The admissions page says $7,000-$15,000 and the scholarship page says $5,000-$15,000.'
