update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International undergraduate direct costs 2026-27: tuition $36,250, housing $4,910, food $6,650, general fee $1,320, technology fee $500, academic fee $360, international student fee $400 = $50,390 per year (double room, meal plan). Required fees $2,580 include the $400 international fee. Books (flat textbook fee $365 per semester per the new-student checklist) and travel are not in the total. Private university: one tuition rate for all students. The F-1 financial guarantee must cover the total minus any scholarship; add $6,000 for a spouse and $4,000 per child; No international need-based aid was found. ORU lists Quest Whole Leader scholarships (up to full tuition; Quest event essay and interview), an International Quest Whole Person Scholarship for international undergraduates who receive Quest (amount not published), a ''Scholarship for New Nations'' for students from countries ORU has never enrolled (no amount), and a renewable $9,250 ApplyBoard award for ApplyBoard-referred students. ORU emails scholarship decisions with the admission decision. ORU reports 100% of full-time residential undergraduates receive scholarship or grant aid.'
