update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UO 2026-27 estimated cost of attendance for a nonresident: tuition and fees $47,466 (resident $17,475), on-campus housing and food $18,183, books $1,434, miscellaneous $2,673 plus transportation $1,500 (entered together as other). Excludes the one-time $570 matriculation fee; first-years must live on campus. Tuition is locked for up to five years (Oregon Guarantee). Health insurance for international students is not itemized; Applicants who apply by Jan. 15 are automatically considered for General University Scholarships (no amounts published on the international pages). Application-based: International Cultural Service Program (ICSP) partial tuition scholarship (need, merit, cultural service; renewable), a work-study program of 50+ awards of $1,000-$4,500, and Division of Global Engagement endowed scholarships of about $1,000-$12,000. In the Common Data Set, 40 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $15,792. Conditional admission with UO Global Welcome (intensive English) is offered; no pathway fee is published on the pages checked.'
