update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'PLU''s 2026-2027 international student expense estimate: tuition and fees $55,760; room and meals $14,670; health insurance, books and personal expenses $4,491; total $74,921, which is the amount of the required financial guarantee minus the scholarship in the admission letter; College Navigator estimated expenses 2024-2025 for beginning undergraduates (tuition and fees; on-campus food and housing). Superseded for international students by the cycle-file cost; International Merit Awards of $8,000-$32,000 per year (first-year and transfer, no application). Stackable: Housing Grant $2,500/yr for living on campus, Visit Scholarship $1,000/yr, Presidential Scholarship (3.8 weighted GPA plus leadership, apply by Dec. 1; variable amount), Artistic Achievement Awards $1,000-$7,500 (audition), Alumni Dependent $1,000; International Access Grant $2,000 for Nordic-country students. PLU says students should expect to pay at least half or more of tuition plus all living costs themselves; no need-based aid for international students is described.'
