update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Tuition page ''Costs (2026-2027)'', per term, 12-18 credits: in-state tuition $4,169 (tuition + fees $6,262.50); out-of-state/international tuition $6,254 (tuition + fees $8,824.50), so fees are $2,570.50 per term for out-of-state/international. The page gives no annual figures; the annual values here are two terms (semester calendar) x the per-term amounts: tuition $8,338 in-state and $12,508 out-of-state/international, fees $5,141. The page shows a single combined ''out-of-state/international'' rate. Housing and food = housing $8,100 + food $4,790 from the cost-of-attendance page, which does not name a year and shows different tuition ($11,574) and fees ($4,224) for out-of-state, so confirm with the university. Scholarships may lower the tuition rate (see the aid notes); The international pages say students may be eligible for financial aid, scholarships, grants and student employment, and that first-year international students are eligible for housing and need-based scholarships (no amounts). The FAQ describes an undergraduate academic scholarship (minimum 2.5 GPA, kept while a 2.5 GPA is maintained) that reduces tuition to the rate non-resident Pennsylvanians pay; its dollar value is not given and the 2026-27 tuition page lists one combined out-of-state/international rate.'
