update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Costs page, 2026-27, per year (2 x semester amounts): nonresident flat-rate tuition including campus fees $10,114 per semester = $20,228 (resident $4,442 per semester = $8,884); residence hall living estimate $5,317 per semester = $10,634 (no meal plan is listed); books and supplies $500 per semester = $1,000. International table adds sickness/accident insurance $2,661 and orientation/SEVIS compliance $80 (extra fees $2,741), for an estimated international academic-year total of $34,603. International students are charged the nonresident rate; Gorilla International Scholarship for new international freshmen and transfers in degree programs: up to $6,000 per year by GPA (3.8-4.0 $6,000; 3.6-3.79 $5,000; 3.4-3.59 $4,000; 3.2-3.39 $3,000; 2.7-3.19 $2,000), a tuition waiver for up to four years of full-time enrollment, rescindable if cumulative GPA falls below 3.0, not valid in summer. English test scores, activities and need are also factors; no deadline is printed. An International Academic Excellence Scholarship also exists (no amount listed). The Common Data Set marks both need-based and non-need-based institutional aid as available to nonresidents.'
