update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International figures are PSU''s 2026-27 estimate for a 9-month year at 12 credits a quarter: tuition $25,632 ($712 a credit base rate; engineering and business pay up to $782.60), fees plus mandatory health insurance $5,775 (insurance is $1,189 a quarter), housing and meals $17,445, books $750, transportation $828 plus personal $1,383. The $13,593 resident and $36,249 nonresident amounts are PSU''s all-in tuition and fees estimate at about 16 credits a term and are on a different basis; All admitted undergraduate international students are automatically considered for merit scholarships of up to $10,000 per year. The International Achievement Scholarship pays $3,000 to $10,000 a year for up to 12 terms for first-years (typical entering GPA 3.25+; no separate application). The University Honors Laurels Scholarship adds up to $3,000 a year for students admitted to the Honors College. Awards apply to tuition and require 12 credits a quarter.'
