update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'PFW international undergraduate estimate for 2026-27 (nine months): tuition and fees $25,161 (one combined figure), living $13,108 (based on a 4-bed, 2-bath on-campus apartment; on-campus living is not required), other $7,196 (books, health insurance, personal), total I-20 cost $45,465. The page says to expect 2-3 percent yearly increases. In-state and out-of-state tuition for 2026-27 not recorded; Automatic PFW academic scholarships (no separate application; minimum 2.5 GPA, full-time, renewable). The out-of-state first-time beginner table, which the page says includes international students, pays per year: GPA 3.5+ $3,000, 3.0-3.49 $2,000, 2.5-2.99 $500. International students submit final transcripts by the end of the first term. The page cites students beginning fall 2022 and later; no international need-based aid is described.'
