update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'PNW cost page, undergraduate full-time (12-18 credits), fall 2026 + spring 2027: tuition and fees $8,672 Indiana / $13,376 non-Indiana / $20,814 international. On-campus housing and food $10,076; other estimates are transportation $2,212 and personal expenses $2,000 ($4,212 together, shown as other costs); books and supplies $608. The total cost of attendance is the sum of the international tuition and these listed components. Mandatory university health insurance for international students is not priced on this page. The international admissions page estimates about $37,000 for one undergraduate year for the I-20; First-year and transfer applicants are automatically considered for the PNW Academic Achievement Scholarship (based on high school GPA, no application, renewable up to 4 years with a 3.0 GPA and 24 credits per year). The page publishes no award amounts and does not say whether international students are eligible, so no international merit policy is recorded. The old PNW English Language Program (intensive English) pages now redirect to the international admissions page, and no conditional-admission pathway is published for international undergraduates.'
