update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Bursar 2026-27 full-time rates (12-18 credits), Radford main campus. Out-of-state undergraduate tuition $22,892 a year; the international admissions page says international tuition equals the out-of-state rate. Required fees for out-of-state students $4,970 (technology $120 + comprehensive $4,382 + capital $468; in-state students pay $4,502 and in-state tuition is $8,894). Room and board is a multiple-occupancy residence hall room ($7,332) plus the Highlander Residential meal plan ($5,866). Common Data Set nonresident aid (both need-based and non-need-based boxes ticked): 55 nonresidents, average $11,556, but the printed total of $1,120,934 does not equal 55 x $11,556, so the count and average may not be consistent. Books and other costs are not published on the pages reviewed. The international Minimum Funding table (labeled 2025-26 in search results) shows a $45,858 total whose line items add to $47,880; International freshmen and transfers are automatically considered for a merit scholarship of $6,000 to $10,000 based on the academic record in the application; no separate aid application. Radford University Foundation scholarships have applications open Nov. 1 to Feb. 5. International students are not eligible for federal aid. The international pages describe only merit awards, while the Common Data Set ticks both need-based and non-need-based institutional aid as available to nonresidents (55 recipients, average $11,556). Proof of funds for one full year is required; the Minimum Funding table shows tuition and fees $27,682, housing $7,332, meals $5,866 and miscellaneous $7,000, with a printed total of $45,858 that does not match the line items.'
