update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27; room-only $9,470, board-only $5,600). Only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 126 nonresident undergraduates received it, average $26,565. URI''s international page says merit awards have historically ranged $8,750 to $15,000 per year (those are first-year awards; the average above covers all years and may include other awards); No need-based aid for international students. All applicants are automatically considered for partial-tuition merit scholarships through the Common App (no separate application), renewable yearly with a minimum GPA; they do not cover room, board or fees. Qualified students have historically received $8,750 to $15,000 per year. Dec. 1 is the priority scholarship date. In the Common Data Set, 126 nonresidents received the college''s own non-need aid, average $26,565.'
