update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'RMU rates for fall 2026 and spring 2027: flat-rate undergraduate tuition (12-18 credits) $18,545 per semester ($37,090 per year); engineering and nursing flat rate is $20,400 per semester. Required fees are the university services fee $595, recreation fee $125, student government fee $20 and residence hall fee $5 per semester, times two. International student fee $325 per semester ($650 per year, shown as the international fee). Housing and food are a standard double room $3,555 plus the all-access meal plan $3,230 per semester, times two. Not included: $200 orientation fee, book bundle fee $30 per credit, health insurance, travel. RMU scholarships for international freshmen ($11,000-$28,000, see aid notes) lower the net price; Academic scholarships are offered to undergraduate international students at the point of acceptance, based on weighted high school GPA (international freshmen): $28,000 for 3.8+, $26,000 for 3.40-3.79, $23,000 for 3.10-3.39, $19,000 for 2.70-3.09, $13,000 for 2.50-2.69, $11,000 below 2.50. The page does not label the amounts as per year; it says full-time students may keep institutional scholarships for up to four years with an overall 2.0 GPA (fully online students are not eligible). A NACES transcript evaluation with a US GPA is required if the transcript has none. No international need-based aid is described.'
