update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Full-time undergraduate tuition per academic year (12-18 credits per semester) for most colleges, $24,197 for 2026-27 (performing arts music/theatre programs $35,086); the general and student activity fees are included in tuition for full-time undergraduates. Other per-semester charges include the CTA U-Pass $123 and student health fee $27.06 (not summed here). On-campus housing ranges from $10,000 to $19,130 per academic year depending on the room, and meal plans are separate; the international page estimates $12,000 for living expenses and still lists undergraduate tuition at $23,100; International students cannot receive U.S. federal or state aid and must show they can pay all expenses. Roosevelt says it offers no full scholarships to international students but gives limited merit scholarships to graduate and undergraduate students; contact the admission counselor for eligibility. Award amounts are not published.'
