update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (academic year 2024-25): in-state tuition $14,222, out-of-state $33,734, required fees $3,028 (College Navigator shows the same, $36,762 out-of-state with fees). Room and board, books and total are College Navigator 2024-25 on-campus figures (total is the out-of-state on-campus cost; in-state $39,200); the Common Data Set food-and-housing line reads $16,074. Only the college''s own non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 31 nonresidents received it (average $7,467); The Common Data Set shows no need-based aid from the college''s own funds for nonresidents; non-need-based aid from the college''s own funds is available (31 nonresidents received it, average $7,467 in the Common Data Set year). The Newark scholarships page (Chancellor''s Scholarship up to $5,000 a year, Carr Scholarship) lists U.S. citizen, national or permanent-resident eligibility and does not mention F-1 students, so no published international scholarship was confirmed (merit scholarships are not shown).'
