update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International page (2026-27): block tuition $14,280 for 12-18 credits per semester, housing and meals $13,000 (optional), miscellaneous $2,640 including mandatory health insurance; estimated total $29,920 (excludes the $1,220 books estimate). Out-of-state and international students have a standard tuition rate of $24,000 that the Red & White Scholarship reduces to $14,280 automatically. No fees for freshmen and sophomores; professional fees apply to select juniors and seniors; First-year costs for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set: one flat block tuition of $14,280 is listed for every residency (it includes the Red & White Scholarship that SVSU applies to out-of-state and international students); no required fees. The Common Data Set shows 245 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid (average $11,403); All applications are reviewed for scholarships with no separate application; awards renew with satisfactory progress. Red & White Award (largest; cuts international tuition from $24,000 to the resident rate of $14,280), President''s International Scholarship ($1,000-$5,000 per year, competitive), Global Bridge Scholarship ($1,000-$5,000 per year), YES/FLEX Alumni Scholarship ($1,500 per year), GAC Pathway Scholarship ($2,000 one time). In the Common Data Set, 245 nonresidents received institutional aid, average $11,403.'
