update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'University Campus undergraduate, full-time, living on campus, per year (Saint Leo''s own cost sheet): tuition $35,000; average housing $9,306 + 19-meal plan $7,520; fees $1,880 (student services $1,100 + activity $280 + one-time orientation $500); books $1,110; miscellaneous $2,772 + transportation $2,988 = $5,760 (federal loan fees of $92 not counted). Total cost of attendance $60,668 as printed. Health insurance ($1,937) is extra unless waived. Figures are for the residential University Campus program (not online/WorldWide), taken from Saint Leo''s cost sheet because no CDS was found; International students are not eligible for U.S. federal aid; the international page points to merit and university scholarships (ask the admissions counselor) and outside funding. The 2026-27 first-year University Campus awards are listed as ''up to'' $24,000 (Presidential), $21,000 (Dean''s), $20,000 (Excellence), $18,000 (University) and $15,000 (Campus); the page does not say how they are awarded to international students (the Catholic Promise and Local Promise awards require U.S. citizenship or Florida residency). Students become eligible to apply for Saint Leo grants and scholarships after paying the $500 deposit.'
