update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Saint Mary''s own 2026-27 cost of attendance for a full-time, on-campus, non-nursing undergraduate: tuition $61,416 (12-18 units per semester) + fees $636 (student body $216, student enhancement $320, student experience $100) + food and housing $18,900 + books $1,304 + personal expenses $3,970 and transportation $1,386 ($5,356 together, shown as other costs) = $87,612 as printed. Nursing (BSN) tuition is $76,770, total $102,330. The tuition figure is the sticker price before merit aid. In the Common Data Set 2023-24 (aid year 2022-23), 64 undergraduate degree-seeking nonresidents received institutional aid, average $51,482 (total $3,294,877); the aid policy checkboxes are not readable as text; International first-year merit scholarships are decided at acceptance, need no separate form, and are automatically applied for four consecutive years of full-time study (renewal depends on satisfactory academic progress). The international scholarships page says awards range from $2,000 to $38,000 per academic year; the international admissions page says $2,000 to $29,000. The page lists no per-award table. Departmental scholarships of $5,000 per year are available to selected incoming first-years. The pages do not say whether international students can receive need-based aid.'
