update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Saint Peter''s Student Accounts, 2026-27 College of Arts & Sciences full-time flat rate $20,885 per semester ($41,770 per year, 12-18 credits); comprehensive fee $1,400 per year; one rate for all students (no separate non-resident or international rate listed). First-year double room $7,800 per year (Millennium or Whelan Hall); meal plans $3,990-$7,070 per year. Room and board total, books and other expenses are not summed because they depend on the housing and meal plan chosen. College Navigator 2024-25 estimates: books and supplies $1,000, on-campus food and housing $17,794, off-campus food and housing $7,500; FAQ: international undergraduates are eligible for scholarships (up to 4 years or 120 credits) based on school marks and test scores, but there are no full scholarships for international students; the Dean of International Enrollment holds the current list. The freshman merit table (awarded at admission by GPA: $20,000 to $30,000 a year, Presidential full tuition) is not labeled domestic-only, but the page does not say it applies to international students, so confirm. Need-based aid for internationals is not described.'
