update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2026-27 undergraduate tuition and fees combined: $13,089.60 in-state, $20,719.20 out-of-state, $15,034.20 NEBHE tuition break; room and board $16,183 (double room in Peabody or Bowditch Hall plus 7-day Silver dining plan). No separate international rate is published; international students are not residents, so the out-of-state rate is likely, but the page does not say so, so no international tuition is shown. Books and supplies were $1,200 in 2024-25 (College Navigator); No international merit scholarship or international aid page was found on Salem State''s official sites. The financial aid page describes only Massachusetts programs (MASSGrant Plus, ''Remarkable Salem State Difference'' for in-state students) that do not apply to nonresident international students. Treat aid for international freshmen as unconfirmed. ESL pathway: complete core level 5+ of Salem State''s American Language and Culture Institute (Pearson Progress Test 49+ and a letter from the IELP director) as an alternative to a test score; the ALCI page says no TOEFL or IELTS is needed for students who pass its core level curriculum.'
