update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27): in-state tuition $7,320, nonresident tuition $19,470, required fees $4,050 (a comment in the Common Data Set says required fees are included in the total tuition, so the fee line may overlap; confirm with the bursar), on-campus food and housing $11,984 (housing $6,658 + meal plan $5,500). Estimated expenses: books $1,380, transportation $2,004, other $1,792 (transportation and other are shown together as other costs). Per-credit-hour: $244 resident, $654 nonresident. The Common Data Set shows 59 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $17,724 (total $1,045,721); No international-specific scholarship is listed on the pages read. Per the scholarships page, a single competitive SHSU scholarship of at least $1,000 can earn a non-resident tuition waiver for the period it covers. In the Common Data Set (fall 2025), 59 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $17,724; its nonresident aid policy boxes are all ticked, so whether it is need-based or merit is unclear. FAFSA is listed as the form for nonresident aid applicants.'
