update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Computed from published rates: full-time undergraduate tuition $3,419 per semester plus nonresident tuition $471 per unit (Fall 2026 and Spring 2027), assuming 15 units a term; fees from the Bursar page. Room and board is campus housing $15,543 plus food $7,369; other = transportation $1,121 plus personal $2,900 (SJSU 2026-27 budget, marked draft). Total = SJSU''s $37,735 campus-housing budget plus $14,130 nonresident tuition (30 units). International students must also buy CSU-provided health insurance (cost not found); In the Common Data Set, 103 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid (avg $9,127, total $940,096). The tuition and fee fields in the Common Data Set are blank, so costs come from SJSU''s Bursar and financial aid office pages (see cost notes); SJSU''s financial aid office says international students are eligible only for merit-based scholarships; need-based aid is unavailable to them. No amounts or international-specific scholarship names are published on that page. SJSU''s international-programs page also mentions International Gateways, which offers academic and TOEFL preparation courses on campus; no conditional-admission pathway is described on the page.'
