update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year; it marks cost data as of June 2026). Tuition shown is the 15-credit-hour flat annual rate: $9,833 for Illinois residents and domestic nonresidents, $24,581.40 for international students (who may qualify for the in-state rate through the High Achievers Alternate Tuition Rate). Tuition varies by program. The Common Data Set marks both need-based and non-need-based institutional aid as available to nonresidents: 44 nonresidents received it, average $19,488. The 44 count is for all degree-seeking undergraduate nonresidents, not just first-year; High Achievers Alternate Tuition Rate: international freshmen with a 3.5 GPA, or ACT 26, or SAT 1240 pay in-state tuition (about $9,833 vs $24,581 per year in the Common Data Set). The older tuition page lists SAT 1170 instead of 1240; the figures here follow the current international page. Transfers need a 3.0 GPA and 26 credits. The Common Data Set says institutional need-based and non-need-based aid exists for nonresidents (44 degree-seeking undergraduate nonresidents got aid, average $19,488), but the admissions pages do not describe international need-based aid, so it is not yet confirmed.'
