update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'SIUE''s international estimate for 2026-27: tuition $20,531, general student fees $3,069, living expenses $17,370 (includes mandatory health insurance $2,583, food, housing, transportation, books and personal), total funds required $40,970. These figures are before any GEO Award reduction. The in-state tuition rate and room and board are not published on the pages reviewed; International GEO Award: a reduced tuition rate for academically qualified first-time, full-time international undergraduates (the admission application is the GEO application; cited English level TOEFL 79 / IELTS 6.5). For 2026-27 it is valued at $10,676 per year (12 credits per semester), good for up to eight semesters. The GEO+ rule moves international undergraduates to in-state tuition after 24 credits. SIUE''s international scholarship list also names the Meridian Scholarship (full tuition, fees, room and board; priority Nov 15, final Dec 1, new first-years) - the page does not state its eligibility rules for international applicants, so confirm before relying on it.'
