update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International cost matrix 2026-27 (bachelor''s degree, 15 credits, average on-campus room and meals): tuition $12,504 (SRU gives international students a reduced out-of-state rate, about $3,996 below the full non-Pennsylvania rate of $16,500; the international page says about $3,500), fees $3,271, room and meal $10,900, enrollment deposit $90, books $800, personal $1,700 = $29,265; the $1,500 Provost Scholarship brings the I-20 financial verification amount to $27,765. The 2027-28 estimate is $26,934; From the Common Data Set: 62 undergraduate degree-seeking nonresidents received institutional aid, average $1,775 (total $110,038); the Common Data Set text does not show whether it was need- or non-need-based. For 2026-27 the Common Data Set lists tuition $7,994 in-state and $11,992 out-of-state/nonresident, required fees $3,470, food and housing $11,098; the cost figures come from the international cost matrix; International students are not eligible for Title IV funds. All new undergraduate international students receive a non-need-based tuition reduction (about $3,500 per the international page, about $3,996 per the cost matrix) and the $1,500 Provost Scholarship for Global Diversity & Academic Achievement is awarded on admission with no extra application (renewal needs a 3.0 GPA; the reduced tuition needs a 2.5 GPA). A $500 Presidential Award follows after the first year or semester with a 3.5 cumulative GPA. Need-based institutional aid for internationals is not described.'
