update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International estimate used for I-20 issuance: tuition and fees $20,486 (12 credit hours per fall and spring semester), housing and food $9,330, books $1,000, health insurance $3,439 (other), total $34,255. Per-credit-hour undergraduate tuition is $386 in-state and $772 out-of-state for Arts and Sciences, higher in Computing and Allied Health ($802 out-of-state), Business ($822), Engineering ($832) and Nursing ($870); the tuition page''s title says 2025-2026 but the rate tables are headed 2026-2027; Global Freshman Scholars Talent and Ability Scholarship (from fall 2026): competitive, for degree-seeking international freshmen on F-1/H-4/L-2 with a 3.0+ high school GPA; the award is in-state tuition rates, renewable up to four years with a 3.0 GPA each year; no dollar figure is listed. Endowed awards (Carter GlobalUSA, Pitsios, Constantine) need 3.0-3.5 GPAs; apply through JagSPOT. The Common Data Set section on aid to nonresidents is not reliably legible.'
