update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'USD international cost page (30 credits per year; the page does not name the academic year): tuition and fees $13,616, living expenses $9,498, other (books, insurance, discipline fees) $2,400. The page gives no total; $25,514 is the sum of those three lines. The page also mentions an annual tuition fee of $13,299, which does not match its own table. The Common Data Set (2024-25) tuition figures ($7,773 / $11,283) look out of date and are not used; The international cost page lists automatic awards for first-time undergraduates: Coyote Beginnings Scholarship up to $4,000 per year based on high school GPA, and Coyote Beginnings Grant $1,500-$2,500 per year for a qualifying SAT/ACT score (stackable); International Transfer Scholarship $3,000 per year (3.0+ U.S. college GPA). The page does not explicitly say these apply to every international freshman, so confirm with USD. The Common Data Set''s nonresident aid figures looked inconsistent and are not used.'
