update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27): domestic/in-state and out-of-state US tuition $9,150, nonresident (international) tuition $18,000, required fees $1,410, food and housing $12,150. Aid: 467 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $8,011 (the need-based/non-need-based boxes could not be read reliably). SEMO''s cost page shows $600 per credit hour for international students ($19,410 with fees for 30 hours), housing $8,450 + meals $3,570, and a total estimate of $34,452.20 on campus ($29,391 off campus); that page''s housing and meals total $12,020 vs $12,150 in the Common Data Set; Automatic merit awards at admission, no separate application: International Academic Award $8,850 per year for freshmen with a 3.25 high school GPA (it covers the nonresident-minus-domestic tuition gap, estimated at 15 hours per semester; renewable up to 4 years with 2.75 GPA and 24 credit hours per year; also for the IEP pathway), or International Student Scholarship $2,000 per year for a 2.5 GPA. No international need-based aid was found on the scholarships page. Common Data Set: 467 nonresidents received institutional aid, average $8,011.'
