update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'The international materials page says expenses are ''at least $31,618'' per year for undergraduates (tuition, housing, meals, textbook rental and health insurance, excluding travel); it prints no academic year. Before any fee waiver; First-year figures from the Common Data Set for 2025-2026 (the 2026-27 figures are not yet published): in-state tuition $5,777, nonresident alien tuition $18,255 ($897 per credit hour), required fees $3,266, on-campus food and housing $10,200. Aid, also from the Common Data Set (2024-25): 229 degree-seeking nonresident aliens received institutional non-need-based aid (average $15,939, total $3,649,929); Non-resident fee waiver for international beginning freshmen (the admission application is the application): minimum TOEFL 75 iBT, IELTS 6.0 or Duolingo 100, a recognized secondary program with GPA 2.25 or higher, and no developmental coursework. It waives the out-of-state fees, which the page lists as up to $6,238 per semester for 12+ hours. Renewal needs full-time status and good standing. The Southeastern Honor Scholarship is also open to international students (ACT-based; SAT is converted). Common Data Set: 229 nonresident aliens received institutional non-need-based aid averaging $15,939.'
