update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Expected costs 2026-27 (tuition page): undergraduate tuition $243 per credit hour in-state and $569 out-of-state, with per-credit fees (student services $9, health and wellness $4, student infrastructure $13); the page says an out-of-state waiver offsets nonresident tuition so you pay the in-state rate, but it does not say whether international students qualify. 2025-26 catalog lists an international student status maintenance fee of $75. Housing runs $1,660-$3,790 per semester and meal plans $1,580-$2,300 per semester. The college-level figures above are 2024-25 College Navigator numbers; College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $7,530, out-of-state $16,740; on-campus food and housing $7,760, other costs $3,216; the total cost of attendance is the out-of-state on-campus total; The international admissions pages list no scholarships specific to international students. Freshman scholarship programs (Honors, President''s Leadership Class, John Massey Leadership Scholars, Parsons Scholars, General Scholarship) require admission first; amounts and international eligibility are not published on the page read. Federal aid is not available to international students in general.'
