update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Sample yearly cost for a residence hall student: tuition $28,900 (12-16 hours), general fee $1,500, residence hall rent $6,000, food allowance $3,900 = $40,300; commuter total $30,400. Southern says the typical out-of-pocket amount is $11,800 per year after scholarships and grants. The page does not mention separate international fees or health insurance; Southern lists automatic freshman merit awards by GPA and ACT/SAT points (Honors $2,000, Dean $4,000, Presidential $6,000 per year, or 50% tuition at the top band) and a full-tuition award at ACT 33-36 depending on GPA, but the pages do not say whether international students are eligible. The Three-Way church scholarship match is explicitly open to international undergraduates ($500 per year maximum). Federal aid requires U.S. citizenship or eligible status. Ask the admissions office what international applicants receive.'
