update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International undergraduate budget for 2026-27 (Tuition Level 1; Level 2 $30,870 and Level 3 $32,580 depending on major; totals $53,490 / $55,260 / $56,970): tuition $29,100, academic fees $3,390, room and board $14,000, books $1,000, health insurance $3,000 and personal expenses $3,000 (shown together as other). In-state and out-of-state 2026-27 tuition were not found; College Navigator 2024-25 lists tuition and fees of $11,284 in-state and $27,944 out-of-state; All international undergraduates who apply by the deadline are automatically considered for merit scholarships, awarded at admission by high school GPA and renewable for 4 years: USM Scholar (GPA 2.75-2.99) $7,000/year, Dirigo Scholar (3.0-3.49) $11,000/year, Presidential Scholar (3.5+) $11,000/year, plus a one-time $2,000 Presidential Recognition Award (3.5+). A $1,000/year housing scholarship is available to those who indicated interest in on-campus housing. The page lists only merit awards and no need-based aid for international students, so need-based aid is left unconfirmed. An Admissions Pathway Program and Intensive ESOL program are available for students below the direct-entry English scores.'
