update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'In-state and out-of-state tuition are the official 2026-27 resident / non-resident annual rates from the USM freshman admissions page (the non-resident rate includes a $1,000 per semester non-resident fee; both include capital-improvement and activity fees). The rest comes from the International Student and Scholar Services cost page (I-20 budget for fall 2026 admits, which adds required health insurance $2,528 and uses an estimated $12,820 non-resident tuition plus $300 fees): total $34,188 for nine months. From the Common Data Set (2024-25): 241 nonresidents received institutional aid, average $13,787; No scholarship specific to international freshmen was found; the international page says SAT/ACT is required for Freshman Merit Scholarship consideration. The freshman merit scale (GPA and ACT) runs from $1,500 per year to full tuition (ACT 32+ with 3.25+ GPA), and Honors College admits get $3,000 per year for four years. Whether international GPAs are scored for these awards is not stated. From the Common Data Set (2024-25): only non-need-based institutional aid for nonresidents; 241 recipients, average $13,787.'
