update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set, first-year 2026-27 (tuition: in-state $6,622, out-of-state $21,550, nonresident $22,630). Aid, also from the Common Data Set: 608 degree-seeking nonresidents received institutional aid (need-based and/or non-need-based), average $10,264, total $6,240,271. SUU''s international costs page estimates $32,915 per year for a single international undergraduate (tuition $22,630, fees $645, program/course fees $250, books $1,000, personal $2,000, shared room and block-100 meal plan $6,390); International scholarships are awarded automatically on the admission application (no separate application): International Founders'' Scholarship $9,000/yr for 4 years, Deans'' $7,000/yr for 4 years, Centurium $4,000/yr for 4 years. The committee weighs GPA (awardees typically 3.0), citizenship and financial need; international scholarships cannot be combined with other substantial SUU tuition scholarships. The Common Data Set says need-based and non-need-based institutional aid is available to nonresidents.'
