update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2026-27 tuition page: undergraduate tuition $252 per credit hour resident and $582 nonresident ($252 + $330), plus mandatory fees of $29.20 per credit hour and an academic enhancement fee of $15 per hour. Catalog: international students are classed as nonresidents; fees include a $100 international maintenance fee per semester and mandatory health insurance. The Costs and Aid page (undated, accessed 2026-10-26) shows undergraduate annual estimates of $9,131 resident, $16,241 nonresident and $26,608 international, without saying what they include; these do not show the In-State Plus $1 rate. Confirm with SWOSU before relying on either figure; College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $8,469, out-of-state $8,499; on-campus food and housing $7,634, other costs $8,746; the total cost of attendance is the out-of-state on-campus total. International students are classed as nonresidents; see the other cost note for SWOSU''s published international cost estimate; Federal aid is not available to international students. The 2025-26 catalog says SWOSU offers its In-State Plus $1 Program to international students (nonresidents paying in-state tuition plus $1 per credit hour, per SWOSU program materials); the exact rate and whether it is automatic could not be confirmed because SWOSU''s program page could not be loaded. Institutional scholarship eligibility for international students is not stated.'
