update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'St. Edward''s 2026-27: full-time flat tuition $25,749 per term (12-18 hours) = $51,498 a year; comprehensive fee $450 per semester. Housing ($4,382) and meal plan ($3,464) are listed as estimates without a stated period, and health insurance (est. $1,460 per semester) is billed unless waived, so room and board and total cost of attendance are not shown. New first-years must live on campus. The university reports an average first-year tuition after scholarships and grants of $11,486 for 2026-27; Undergraduate international students are considered for academic scholarships through the admission application, and for need-based grants by filing the CSS Profile for international applicants (code 6619, priority Feb. 15). First-year merit scholarships range from $14,000 to $32,000 a year for students admitted through regular admission (not limited to internationals); the Moreau Scholarship (full tuition, one per Holy Cross high school) lists international applicants submitting test or English scores. Not eligible for U.S. federal loans. Whether the university is need-blind or meets full need for internationals is not stated.'
from public.institutions i
