update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Queens campus, living on campus, 2026-27: tuition $56,140 (12-18 credits per semester), fees $1,660, housing $13,728, food $8,230, books $844, loan fees $58, personal $2,110, transportation $1,020 (total $83,790). Business majors in years 3-4 pay a tuition differential. One tuition rate for all students; The FAQ says St. John''s has no financial aid for international students but its merit scholarships are competitive; the admission application automatically determines eligibility. For the fall 2026 entering class merit scholarships were awarded up to $36,000 annually for up to four years (no per-GPA grid is published; test-optional applicants are still considered). Catholic Scholars (separate application, $10,000 per year) and the Catholic School Scholarship ($3,000 per year, automatic) also apply to international students.'
