update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (full 2026-2027 year): tuition $38,404, required fees $1,478, food and housing $13,438; books $1,300. Aid: 55 degree-seeking nonresidents received institutional aid, average $42,263 (total $2,324,499) for the aid year the Common Data Set marks as 2023-24; the Common Data Set does not say whether this is need-based or merit aid; First-time freshmen who apply by Feb. 1 and enroll full-time are automatically considered for academic merit scholarships of $10,000-$26,000 per year; the page does not say whether international students are eligible. The Global Scholars Program gives international students $2,000 per year for academic excellence and cultural understanding (renewed annually). The university reports that nearly 98% of first-time freshmen receive scholarships or institutional grants. Common Data Set: 55 nonresidents received institutional aid, average $42,263.'
