update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2025-2026): in-state tuition $7,761, out-of-state $19,911, required fees $3,467, food and housing $13,940; books $1,206 and other expenses $1,850. No separate international tuition figure is printed in the Common Data Set (the nonresident row is blank); OIP scholarship is $1,000 per year (requires financial need, 2.75 GPA for undergraduates, application due April 30; the page does not say whether new freshmen can apply). Recipients of a competitive scholarship of $1,000 or more may pay Texas resident tuition (page: about $4,500 less per semester). Scholarship funds are limited. Financial proof for the I-20: $39,428, or $28,708 with a scholarship of $1,000 or more.'
