update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (2025-26, first-year): tuition $59,290, required fees $400, on-campus housing $9,741 plus food $8,601; books $850, other costs $1,099. Stetson says an F-1 applicant must show funds for one year of tuition and fees plus about $4,200 for books and other expenses. Non-need-based institutional aid is available to nonresidents and 197 received it; the average of $61,173 reported in the Common Data Set exceeds tuition, so it is not shown; Federal aid is limited to US citizens; international students may apply for Stetson scholarships. Merit scholarships for new first-years are decided by the admissions committee when the application is complete (no separate application): Presidential up to $40,000, Dean''s up to $32,000, Faculty-Merit up to $27,000 per year, renewable for eight semesters. J. Ollie Edmunds Distinguished Scholarship (four years of expenses, selected on leadership) is open to scholars from around the world. The CDS shows 197 nonresident undergraduates received non-need institutional aid.'
