update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2024-25): nonresident tuition $17,320, required fees $1,755, food and housing on campus $17,026. These are 2024-25 figures; 2026-27 rates were not confirmed; All international applicants are considered for scholarships at application, no separate application. Destination Oswego Scholarship: $9,000 per year ($4,500/semester) beginning fall 2027 for full-time first-year students who are international or non-NY residents; must live on campus, keep a 3.0 GPA each semester, renewable up to eight semesters. First-year merit awards by typical HS average: Presidential $6,000 (96+), Dean''s $4,000 (93-95), Merit Plus $2,500 (90-92), Merit $750 (85-89) per year; the page does not say whether international students are eligible for these. The Common Data Set (2024-25) shows 172 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid averaging $6,888 (the aid-type checkbox is unreadable). English pathway: applicants below the minimum can enroll in the English for Academic Purposes (EAP) program through Oxford International Digital Institute, and proof of enrollment can lead to conditional admission; another admissions page says below-minimum students need intensive English study before admission. The international page estimates total cost of attendance at $41,493 per year (year not stated).'
