update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2025-26; it ticks that final 2025-26 costs were not yet available): in-state tuition $5,137, nonresident tuition $18,133, required fees $4,755, on-campus food and housing $10,823 (housing $6,400 + meal plan $4,423). Estimated expenses for residents: books $1,190, transportation $1,315, other $2,007 (transportation and other are counted together as other costs). Per-credit-hour: $171 resident, $604 nonresident. 17 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $1,522 (total $25,867); No international-specific scholarship is listed. Merit scholarships are automatic for at least 50% of admitted first-time students (Presidential $5,000-$12,000 per year, typical profile SAT 1300 / ACT 27 and top 10% rank; Academic Excellence $1,000-$4,000, SAT 1170 / ACT 24, top 20%), but the page does not say international students are eligible. Out-of-state recipients of the competitive merit scholarship pay in-state tuition in the semesters it is disbursed (not summer). The Common Data Set shows 17 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $1,522. Cost of attendance page for out-of-state/international students (dorm): tuition and fees $21,994, food and housing $11,946, books $1,391, transportation $1,390, miscellaneous $2,246 = $38,967 (the table sits under the 2026-27 heading but its header reads ''Academic Year 25-26'').'
