update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, 2026-27 update). Tuition is a weighted average because Temple has differential tuition by school/college (60% of undergraduates pay more). Only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 624 nonresidents received it (avg $17,619; total $10,994,319); FAQ: need-based aid is not available to international students. Merit scholarships for first-year international students range up to $20,000 per year for up to four years (FAQ: $1,000-$20,000); no separate application, the admissions application is the scholarship application. Separate-application awards: #YouAreWelcomeHere (two first-year students per the scholarships page, $20,000/yr) and #WhyUS ($2,000-$10,000/yr). Bridge students keep any earned merit scholarship.'
