update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'College Navigator estimates for full-time beginning undergraduates, 2024-25 (the latest published there): tuition and fees in-state $8,616, out-of-state $22,416; on-campus food and housing $11,150; books $1,600; other expenses $5,811. TSU did not report costs in its 2025-26 Common Data Set (final costs due 7/1/2026) and its 2026-27 tuition schedule is a scanned image, so newer figures could not be read; TSU says to expect 2-5% increases. No separate international tuition rate is stated on the pages reviewed, so out-of-state is the likely rate. For nonresident undergraduates, the Common Data Set shows institutional need-based aid is available; 84 received it, average $19,162, total $1,609,573; Institutional merit scholarships are open to first-time freshmen and international students and are considered automatically once the admission application, official transcript and ACT/SAT scores are in (some awards need a separate application). Amounts per year for out-of-state/international students: Renaissance $8,500 (weighted GPA 3.75+ or ACT 28/SAT 1300+), 1912 Heritage $6,500 (GPA 3.25-3.74 or ACT 25-27/SAT 1200-1290), Torch Scholars $4,500 (GPA 3.0-3.24 or ACT 20-24/SAT 1030-1190). Renewal needs a 3.0 GPA, 15 credits a semester and, as printed, a FAFSA each year, which international students cannot file, so ask TSU how renewal works for them. Only one merit scholarship can be held. The full-ride awards (Presidential, Watkins) are for U.S. citizens. The Common Data Set ticks institutional need-based aid for nonresident undergraduates (84 recipients, average $19,162), but the TSU international pages describe only merit awards. Amounts and criteria are for Fall 2026 entry; Fall 2027 terms are not yet posted.'
from public.institutions i
