update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'TSU ''estimated cost for the 2027-2028 academic year'', on-campus out-of-state column: tuition and fees $21,416, living expenses $19,470, books $1,654, personal $3,222, transportation $2,806 = $48,568 (the same amount international applicants must show). In-state tuition and fees $9,174; in-state living expenses $15,064. TSU does not publish a separate international tuition rate on this page; College Navigator (IPEDS 2024-25): tuition includes required fees; room and board is on-campus; No scholarship specifically for international students was found. Under Texas Education Code 54.213, a non-resident or international student who wins a competitive university scholarship of at least $1,000 can pay the resident tuition rate (must be requested each semester). The catalog says international students seeking a first bachelor''s degree cannot get Pell Grants, Federal Work-Study or Federal Direct Loans.'
