update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year full-year amounts from the Common Data Set; room and board is on-campus housing $8,076 plus meal plan $4,824. The Common Data Set text refers to both 2025-26 and 2026-27, so the year is most likely 2025-26 (IPEDS 2024-25 was $11,450 in-state / $22,930 out-of-state tuition and fees). 1,131 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional need-based or non-need-based aid (avg $22,760, total $25,741,960); nonresident first-years file the International Student''s Financial Aid Application; International students can compete for academic scholarships if admitted by the scholarship deadline. A Texas State competitive or merit scholarship of $1,000+ can bring a nonresident tuition waiver (resident rate; Selective Service registration or exemption and lawful presence required). Need-based Tuition Assistance for Mexican Students (TAMS) and the merit-based Good Neighbor Scholarship (Western Hemisphere) are listed; online-degree students are not eligible for institutional scholarships. The Common Data Set says institutional need-based and non-need-based aid exists for nonresidents (1,131 recipients, avg $22,760).'
