update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'The Common Data Set gives tuition, fees and room and board. International tuition and the total cost of attendance come from Troy''s international tuition page (2026-27 estimate for the Troy campus at 13 credit hours a semester at $746 per credit hour: tuition $19,864, fee $3,250, insurance $1,860, book bag $624, room $7,000, board $4,456, supplies $200 = $37,254; $27,322 after the $9,932 International Trojan Opportunity scholarship). The Common Data Set shows 351 nonresidents received institutional non-need-based aid (average $15,702, total $5,512,833); The International Trojan Opportunity scholarship is for entering international freshmen and transfers enrolled full-time (12+ hours) who meet admission and English requirements; it is applied for through AwardSpring, is renewable for students in good standing, and the cost table shows it as $9,932 a year (page text: ''waive the out-of-state tuition cost''). Troy also lists a Chancellor''s Endowed General Scholarship, an International Student Scholarship and the Lindsey Endowed Scholarship. The Common Data Set reports only non-need-based institutional aid for nonresidents (351 recipients, average $15,702).'
