update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set: in-state $11,970, out-of-state $29,820, nonresident (international) $32,490; required fees $500; on-campus food and housing $14,720. Tuition varies by program. The Common Data Set shows 189 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $18,850 (total $3,562,740); its text does not show whether the aid was need-based or non-need-based; UAB International Scholarship: US $7,500 per year, considered automatically at admission for first-year, full-time degree-seeking students living outside the US who finished secondary school outside the US within 3 years with a 3.0/4.0 GPA, have no prior college work and expect an F-1 visa. First come, first served while funds last; renewable for 4 years; not for students on government scholarships or other external support. Other UAB scholarships use the BSMART application (due April 1). Whether international students can get need-based aid is not stated. INTO UAB pathway programs (for students below direct-entry GPA/English levels): accelerated 1 semester (TOEFL 77, IELTS 6.0, Duolingo 120, GPA 2.0); standard 2 semesters (TOEFL 60, IELTS 5.5, Duolingo 90); comprehensive 3 semesters (TOEFL 50, IELTS 5.0, Duolingo 75).'
