update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees $7,334 in-state / $12,182 out-of-state; on-campus food and housing $10,082. Published total cost on campus is $29,156 out-of-state ($24,308 in-state); the total is not shown because the two differ. International students pay the out-of-state rate (2026-27 per-credit rates are in the aid notes); 2026-27 per-credit-hour rates: out-of-state and international $400 tuition + $106.50 mandatory fees = $506.50 (in-state $334.50), plus $73 per semester (registration and health) and an international Student Services Fee of $350 per semester. Freshman merit scholarships (ACT or GPA based, up to $1,000-$6,000 plus up to a $1,500 housing stipend) and prestigious scholarships (Myles Friedman Honors up to $34,000 over four years, ACT 27 or 3.5 GPA) exist. The international page says international students may apply for Myles Friedman and freshman merit scholarships but not those requiring Pell eligibility. No need-based aid for international students is described.'
