update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UConn 2026-27 estimate for a Stamford campus student living on campus, out-of-state rate (international students are not separately priced on the page): tuition $39,678 (Connecticut resident $17,010); Stamford fees $1,450; Stamford housing estimate $14,578 plus food $6,896; books $1,020; transportation $2,704, personal $1,968 and loan fees $92. Total $68,386 is the page''s out-of-state figure. Health insurance (waivable) is extra; Financial aid is only for U.S. citizens and permanent residents. All applicants are automatically considered for merit scholarships; international-only awards (Global Excellence, Global Distinction, Global Leader) are renewable for 4 years at a fixed amount set each year (the amount is not published); priority date Dec. 1. The Regional Student Success Award is for Connecticut residents only. A student below the English minimum who is otherwise admissible can be offered conditional admission with UConn''s American English Language Institute (UCAELI).'
