update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Schedule of charges 2026-27, 12 credit hours per semester doubled to a year: resident tuition $2,555.28 per semester; non-resident and international tuition $7,691.28 per semester; fees $337.44 service + $585.60 extended access + $96.00 library per semester. The cost-of-attendance page shows a higher all-in figure for tuition and fees ($21,607 per year out-of-state/international, $8,767 in-state), which includes charges not itemized in the schedule. Housing and food, books, other costs (transportation $1,425 plus miscellaneous $2,371) and the total cost of attendance come from the dorm column of that page''s out-of-state/international per-year table. Freshmen must live on campus; the 2024-25 international cost page also lists mandatory F-1 health insurance of $3,147; International Student Merit Scholarship: for F-1 students it applies the in-state tuition rate and can reduce the cost of attendance by $3,000 to $10,000 over two semesters (tuition and fees only; essay and resume required; apply by June 15 for fall; keep 2.5 GPA and 10 volunteer hours). International Student Cultural Scholarship: $1,500 per year ($750 per semester) for F-1/J-1 students on first-come basis, applied to out-of-state tuition and fees; a student can hold only one international scholarship. Need-based aid for international students is not stated.'
