update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set: nonresident tuition 20,400; fees exclude student health insurance. UIS''s cost page (updated 2026-08-31) estimates $9,957 tuition plus $10,038 for nonresidents and a total of about $40,435 on campus for nonresidents. The Common Data Set says institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 52 received it (average $13,083); UIS says financial assistance for international students is limited. First-year, international and transfer applicants are automatically reviewed for merit scholarships (Star Scholar Award $3,000-$7,000/yr by unweighted GPA on the 2025-26 schedule, renewable; Capital Scholars Honors up to $8,000/yr), and donor-funded scholarships (apply early Nov to mid-Feb) are open to international students. The Out-of-State Scholarship is not available to international or UIS Global students. The Common Data Set shows 52 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $13,083.'
