update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'College Navigator (IPEDS) 2024-25 for full-time beginning undergraduates: tuition and fees $9,190 in-state / $21,290 out-of-state; on-campus total $27,316 in-state / $39,416 out-of-state. International students pay the out-of-state rate unless the Out-of-State Warhawk Scholarship ($12,100 a year) applies. Current-year prices were not checked; The Out-of-State Warhawk Scholarship is a fee waiver of $6,050 a semester ($12,100 a year) for first-time, full-time international freshmen (and transfers with 12+ college hours and a 2.5 GPA) who are non-Louisiana residents with a 2.5 high school GPA, SAT English 440 / ACT English 15, SAT Math 430 / ACT Math 16 and the language scores listed on the scholarship page. ULM''s pages mention only merit-based awards for international students; no need-based institutional aid is described. The fee waiver can be combined with domestic-style academic scholarships priced by ACT/SAT.'
