update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs for 2024-2025 from the Common Data Set: in-state tuition $14,208, out-of-state and non-resident $27,744, required fees $682, food and housing $12,854; books $700, other costs $1,310. The Common Data Set shows only institutional non-need-based aid for nonresidents; 30 nonresidents received it, average $5,815. The current International Tuition & Fees page (the page prints no year; checked Aug 2026) lists undergraduate lower-division tuition of $29,002 for 12 credits per semester, with estimated total international expenses of $45,215 (living $11,943, health insurance $2,470, books $800, miscellaneous $1,000); mandatory fees are not included; International first-year students are automatically considered for First-Year Merit Scholarships (no separate application). The June 2025 scholarship page lists Maize & Blue awards of $1,000 to $10,000 per year for 4 years (renewal 2.75 GPA) based on GPA and optional test scores; a GPA-only First-Year Opportunity Scholarship gives $1,000 per year (2.7-3.7 GPA) or $3,000 per year (3.7+). The Aug 2026 tuition page says awards go up to $5,000 a year, so the current amounts need confirming. The True Blue award is described as full in-state tuition. The Common Data Set shows only non-need-based institutional aid for nonresidents (30 recipients, average $5,815).'
