update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Out-of-state (international) on-campus estimate for 2026-27 (12 credits): tuition $36,610, fees $850, housing $11,402 (weighted average) and food $6,080, books $1,200, loan fees $68, transportation $500, miscellaneous $900 (total $57,610). Required student health insurance for international students is $3,617 (ISSO expense page) and is not in the total. New England regional students pay a reduced rate; From the Common Data Set (2024-25): institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 120 undergraduate degree-seeking nonresidents received it (average $12,606, total $1,512,741); Out-of-state, national and international first-year applicants of exceptional merit are considered for scholarships of $8,000 to $20,000 per year (type and amount depend on the applicant pool; renewable for up to eight semesters with a 3.0 GPA). No separate application: eligibility is decided at admission and notified with the acceptance letter. The Immersive Scholars Program adds $4,000 for research, community work or study abroad. International students are expected to show sufficient funds.'
