update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Spartan Central undergraduate annual cost table: tuition and fees $7,864 in-state / $25,347 out-of-state (international students pay the out-of-state rate); standard double room $6,433 + unlimited meal plan $5,209 = $11,642. The table does not print its year; it sits next to the 2026-27 fee schedule links. The tuition shown is the in-state figure; College Navigator estimated expenses for beginning undergraduates, 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $7,661, out-of-state $24,012; books $850; on-campus food and housing $10,688; other $3,386. The current-cycle cost block (2026-27) overrides these; Limited merit-based International Student Scholarships of $3,000-$6,000 per year for new degree-seeking international students with a minimum 3.5 GPA, renewable for one more year at a 3.5 GPA; no separate application. Notified in March and June (fall). Additional financial aid is not available to non-US citizens.'
