update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set: in-state tuition $1,000 and out-of-state/nonresident $7,000 (NC Promise tuition); housing $6,094 + food $6,026 = $12,120. The Common Data Set says only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 66 nonresident undergraduates received it (average $6,293, total $415,326). The tuition shown is the in-state figure; F-1 students get no federal aid. Institutional scholarships are matched through the BraveAssist portal after a general application; Early Action (Dec 1 for fall) is the merit-scholarship consideration date. No international scholarship amounts are published. The Common Data Set shows 66 nonresident undergraduates got institutional non-need-based aid, average $6,293.'
