update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UNLV cost page (2026-27, 15 credits, two semesters): the tuition figures already include required fees and a one-time $200 new-student fee; international (F-1) $31,710 includes a $145-per-semester international fee; mandatory health insurance for international students is estimated separately. Housing and food are on-campus housing $7,424 + food $6,024; other costs are transportation $1,360 + miscellaneous $3,304. Estimated nonresident total cost living on campus $50,284; Admitted international undergraduates may be considered for merit-based scholarships of $5,000-$7,000 per year (once a year, fall entry only; must be admitted before the priority deadline and complete UNLV''s Alternative Need Form). No need-based aid for international students is described, so that is left unconfirmed.'
