update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set: in-state $11,585, out-of-state/nonresident $34,734, required fees $1,639.80 (rounded), food and housing $12,471. International students pay the nonresident rate unless they receive a scholarship (see aid); All undergraduate applicants are automatically considered; one award only, no stacking. International Amigo Scholarship: in-state tuition rate (about $27,000/yr value; fees not included) for 3.5 GPA, or 3.0 GPA plus ACT 26 / SAT 1240, or 3.25 GPA with 30+ transferable credits. Leadership Scholarship: about $17,000/yr, 3.0 GPA. Beca Mexico (Mexican citizens): 1.5x resident tuition, 2.5 GPA. Renewable up to four years with 15 credit hours and a 2.5 GPA each semester. UNM lists 2027-28 tuition and fees of $11,700 (Amigo), $20,893 (Leadership) and $38,850 (no scholarship). The page does not mention need-based aid for international students, so that is left unconfirmed.'
