update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year full-year amounts from the Common Data Set (nonresident tuition equals out-of-state $20,823; per credit hour $685 nonresident vs $280 in-state). The Common Data Set marks 2026-27 costs as not yet available, so these are most likely 2025-26 amounts. The Common Data Set says only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 1,075 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received it (average $5,928). The admission factor rows for test scores, essay and recommendations were left unmarked, so they are not shown; UNT Excellence Scholarship ($2,000-$12,000 a year by class rank and unweighted GPA, renewable up to 4 years, +$1,000 bonus for SAT 1350/ACT 30) and the $1,000-a-year UNT Achievement Scholarship are automatic for first-time freshmen admitted by the priority date; the page states they apply to international students too. International recipients may get a Texas competitive scholarship waiver covering the difference between in-state and out-of-state tuition (Selective Service requirement applies where relevant). The CDS reports institutional aid for nonresidents as non-need-based only.'
