update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'IPEDS College Navigator 2024-25 first-time undergraduate expenses: tuition amounts include required fees; on-campus food and housing $11,228. Newer 2026-27 charges are on UTA''s Student Accounts tuition charts and were not read; Every incoming freshman is reviewed for the Maverick Academic Scholarship ($1,000-$8,000 a year for fall, renewable up to three more years; SAT/ACT optional). For 2026-27, non-residents receiving the $8,000 Maverick award (or Presidential Honors $13,000 / Presidential $10,000) are eligible for a Non-Resident Tuition Waiver (in-state rates); lower awards carry an International Grant of up to $10,000 ($4,000 award), $8,000 ($2,000 award) or $5,000 ($1,000 award). Waivers and grants are not guaranteed and depend on funding. UTA''s pages did not state whether need-based aid exists for international students.'
