update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set (first-year, on-campus; it labels this block 2026-2027): non-resident tuition equals out-of-state tuition, $18,727 for 30 credits. Its estimated on-campus expenses also list transportation $1,778 and other expenses $1,872. Certain programs carry additional course fees. College Navigator (2024-25) showed out-of-state total cost of attendance $40,840 on campus; Freshman merit scholarships are automatic at admission, no application: Falcon Elite $4,000/yr (3.90+ unweighted GPA), Excellence $3,000 (3.70-3.89), Achievement $2,000 (3.35-3.69), Recognition $1,000 (3.25-3.34); renewable up to 4 years with 12 credits per term and a 2.50 GPA. The scholarship pages do not say whether international students qualify, and the 2025-26 catalog states ''The University has no financial aid available for international students.'' The Common Data Set (as copied from the PDF text; the need-based or non-need-based box was unreadable) shows 103 undergraduate nonresidents with institutional aid, average $6,683.'
