update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year, full-time costs from the Common Data Set, as printed under the 2026-2027 heading: in-state tuition $7,232, nonresident tuition $22,680 (about $756/credit hour x 30), required fees $2,504, on-campus food and housing $13,756 (housing $9,074 + meal plan $4,684). Its estimates for residents: books $2,920, transportation $1,424, other $1,714 (the other costs shown combine transportation and other). UT Tyler publishes no separate international tuition rate on the pages checked, so international tuition is shown as the nonresident rate; The international scholarship page (headed 2022-2023, so confirm amounts) lists: Honors Scholars $10,000 (3.75+ GPA, Dec. 1, interview, four-year eligibility); Patriot Scholarship $1,000-$5,000 (3.5+ GPA, priority Dec. 1, final March 1); Academic Excellence Scholarship $2,000 (top 25% with 3.0 GPA, or 3.5 GPA for international/unranked students; no application). Awards must be confirmed by May 1 and funding is limited. CDS nonresident aid figures are blank in the PDF.'
