update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International undergraduate estimate for Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 (9 months, Logan): tuition and fees $29,222, international student fee $250, living expenses $8,148, personal expenses $8,442, total $46,062. The $29,222 tuition-and-fees estimate is higher than CDS tuition plus required fees ($25,717 + $793), and the page does not itemize the difference (it notes differential tuition and program fees may apply). Proof of one year of funds is required for the I-20; First-year costs for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set: in-state tuition $8,272, out-of-state and nonresident tuition $25,717, required fees $793, on-campus food and housing $9,746, books $856, transportation $2,648, other $1,628. Tuition varies by program; The international undergraduate scholarship list shows the Afton B. Tew Scholarship ($1,000, 1-4 years), the Kim Nam Kyun Scholarship ($2,000, 1-4 years, must be admitted to apply), an International Nonresident Tuition Waiver (HB118, amount varies, 1-4 years) and an International Alumni Legacy Nonresident Waiver (amount varies, 1 year). The Common Data Set checks both need-based and non-need-based institutional aid for nonresidents and reports 1,564 recipients averaging $15,299, but that count is far larger than the 218 nonresident undergraduates in its enrollment figures, so it is not used as an international figure. Eligibility rules for each award were not reviewed.'
from public.institutions i
