update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'College Navigator 2024-25: tuition and fees in-state $9,987, out-of-state $19,827; on-campus food and housing $9,728, other expenses $3,918. The total cost of attendance shown is the published out-of-state on-campus total (the rate an international student would normally face; UTRGV does not publish a separate international tuition rate on the pages checked); No automatic international merit scholarship amounts were found. International Student Services lists a $1,000 summer need-based grant for continuing students, the state-run Good Neighbor Scholarship (tuition exemption for students from Western Hemisphere countries other than Cuba and the U.S., selected by the Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board), and ''I am a Buddy'' awards of $500-$700 per semester for enrolled students. UTRGV''s I-20 estimate for a full-time overseas undergraduate paying non-resident tuition is $41,668 living independently (2026-27 table).'
