update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'IPEDS College Navigator 2024-25 first-time undergraduate expenses: tuition amounts include required fees; on-campus food and housing $14,912. The Common Data Set did not report costs. From the Common Data Set 2024-25: 340 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid (avg $6,646, total $2,259,506); it did not mark whether the aid was need- or non-need-based; International students are not eligible for federal aid. The merit-based Distinguished Presidential Scholarship for fall freshmen admitted by Jan. 15 pays $500-$6,000 a year by class rank and SAT/ACT (e.g. top 20% with 1170 SAT / 24 ACT: $2,500; top 25% with 1150 / 24: $500; applicants without scores go to committee review) and is valued up to $24,000 over four years; nonresident/international recipients of at least $1,000 a year get a nonresident tuition waiver while eligibility is maintained. The need-based International Student Grant requires F-1/J-1 status and full-time enrollment; the Good Neighbor Program covers tuition for eligible Western Hemisphere countries (its current funding status is unconfirmed).'
