update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'From the Common Data Set 2023-24 (2024-25 costs, firm and final): in-state tuition and fees $8,531, out-of-state and international $16,213 per year; on-campus food and housing $8,548; books $1,200; other expenses $2,000 plus $1,500 transportation. College Navigator lists out-of-state tuition and fees of $16,446 for 2024-25. No 2026-27 international cost page could be read, so these are older figures. Titan Global Scholars can cut the nonresident tuition by 50-100 percent; Titan Global Scholars: all international applicants sponsored for an F-1 or J-1 visa by UW Oshkosh are automatically considered (no separate application). Nonresident tuition discount by cumulative GPA: 3.75-4.00 = 100 percent (Black and Gold Elite), 3.00-3.74 = 75 percent (Advantage), 2.50-2.99 = 50 percent (Access); worth about $16,000 to $32,000+ over four years. Requires full-time degree enrollment (12+ credits) and a 2.5 cumulative GPA to keep it; lasts up to 150 attempted credits. The FAQ also says admitted students get a chance to apply for a need-based scholarship during the immigration application, but no amounts or rules are published, so need-based aid for international students and the aid policy are not shown.'
