update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'International Certification of Finances Form 2026-27: tuition and fees $19,748, housing and meals (double room, 21 meals a week) $8,759, required UW international student health insurance $2,234, less $5,120 renewable tuition remission = $25,621 total estimated amount. Tuition rows 9,440 (Wisconsin resident) and 18,330 (other non-resident) are from the tuition page for tuition only (room/meals/total there use a different meal plan); The 2026-27 international Certification of Finances Form lists a ''Renewable Tuition Remission'' of $5,120 off the first-year estimate (stay full-time with a 2.5 cumulative GPA). Domestic first-year Soar Achievement guaranteed awards are $1,000 (3.3 GPA), $1,500 (3.75) and $2,000 (4.0); the pages do not say whether international students receive them. International students are not eligible for U.S. federal or state aid.'
