update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UW-Stout international undergraduate estimate for 2026-27 (30 credits): tuition and fees $21,785; housing $5,340 plus food and living expenses $3,792 (shown as housing and food, $9,132); mandatory health insurance $2,010 (shown as other costs); total $32,927. The page expects about 8 percent yearly increases. ESL Institute students: tuition and fees $12,299, total $23,441. Domestic in-state and out-of-state tuition is not shown; All international degree applicants are automatically considered for the International Student Tuition Scholarship: up to $5,000 per year for first-year and transfer students with a cumulative GPA of 3.0 or higher (4.0 scale), renewable each semester (15 credits per semester, 3.0 GPA, global-involvement requirement). Not available for ESL Institute courses. A limited number of #YouAreWelcomeHere scholarships (50% of nonresident tuition, excluding fees, renewable up to four years) need a separate application; the two awards cannot be combined. ESL pathway: the ESL Institute (five levels) admits with no minimum English test score; conditional degree students must finish the high-advanced level with a 2.0 ESL GPA before starting degree courses.'
from public.institutions i
