update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'UW-Superior international page, 2026-27 estimate for full-time on-campus students: nonresident tuition and fees $18,155; most affordable double room with a 13-meal plan $7,945 (shown as housing and food; the page suggests $1,285 more for extra meals); required health insurance $2,255 (shown as other costs); books about $1,090; orientation fee $255 once. The total cost of attendance shown is the page''s minimum funding to show for an F-1 visa without a scholarship ($32,385; it also includes personal expenses). With the NTW scholarship the page''s total is $22,710 or $20,510; Nonresident Tuition Waiver (NTW): automatic for qualifying international degree-seeking undergraduates, no separate application; more than 90 percent of international students receive it. First-year GPA 2.90-3.39 waives $5,900 per year (tuition and fees then $12,255); GPA 3.40+ (NTW Scholar) waives $8,100 per year ($10,055). Renewable up to four years. Separately, two #YouAreWelcomeHere scholarships of $8,400 per year are awarded each fall (GPA 3.5+, separate application, cannot be combined with NTW). No need-based aid for international students is described.'
