update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2026-27 tuition and fees: $9,235 Wisconsin resident, $19,336 nonresident, $19,756 international (international page). The international room-and-food estimate is $8,830. Required UW System international student health insurance adds $2,180 a year, and personal expenses are estimated at $3,510; the $34,276 total (tuition and fees, housing and food, insurance, personal) is the amount the page lists as proof of funds for an I-20; Automatic-by-GPA international freshman scholarships, renewable for up to 8 semesters: Merit $2,000 per year (equivalent GPA 2.5+), Distinction $4,000 (3.0+), Excellence $6,000 (3.4+). Not open to fully sponsored students. Renewal needs active F-1 status, a 2.5 GPA at UW-Whitewater and involvement in at least three intercultural programs or organizations each semester. A separate $1,000-per-year Business and Computer Science International Student Provost Scholarship goes to international undergraduates in those majors. Whether need-based aid exists for international students is not stated.'
from public.institutions i
