update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'VCU 2026-27 table: tuition and fees combined $17,963 (Virginia resident) / $41,127 (non-resident), based on 15 credits per semester; room $9,259 (first-year double in Rhoads Hall) plus dining $6,630. New first-years add a $250 one-time transition fee. Major-specific fees extra; Out-of-state academic scholarships are open to international students: four-year awards of $10,000 (3.00 high school GPA) to $15,000 (4.00) per year, renewable up to three more years, no separate application; GPA tiers $10,000 / $11,000 (3.25) / $12,000 (3.50) / $14,000 (3.75) / $15,000 (4.00). University-level Provost and Deans'' scholarships cover in-state costs only. From the Common Data Set (2024-25): 148 undergraduate nonresidents were awarded institutional aid, average $11,243; whether need-based aid exists for nonresidents could not be read from the Common Data Set check boxes.'
