update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Vermont State 2026-27 full-time annual, standard programs: Vermont resident tuition $11,088; out-of-state and international $22,152 (engineering/technology $27,840, nursing $28,584, dental/radiologic science $31,224); in-person institution fee $1,704; international student fee $310; standard on-campus housing $8,682 plus food plan $5,782; personal $3,600 plus transportation $2,910. Books are listed as $1,000-$1,680, so no books figure is shown; health insurance $2,174 is waivable. A total cost of attendance is not published; International Student Scholarship: competitive, up to $3,500 per year, for non-citizens and non-residents enrolling full-time in a first bachelor''s degree; renewable up to four years of continuous full-time enrollment with satisfactory progress; the committee weighs academic and extracurricular credentials; no deadline is printed. The financial aid page says institutional merit scholarships for international and out-of-state students are awarded from the admissions application. International need-based aid is not described. Conditional admission: students below regular English minimums (TOEFL 55 / IELTS 5 / Duolingo 90) start in the in-person Castleton Campus Pathway Program for English Language Learners.'
