update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'Tuition and fees are from the Common Data Set (2026-27); other costs are transportation $1,716 plus personal $1,968. The total cost of attendance shown is WSU International Programs'' estimate for an international undergraduate for fall plus spring (tuition and fees $33,087, books $900, medical insurance $4,290, living $17,246, other $3,684; page does not name the year). The Common Data Set says only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 216 nonresident undergraduates received it (avg $10,094); International students are automatically considered for scholarships on admission. The International Academic Award is guaranteed to high-achieving first-year admits: $4,000 per year tuition waiver for GPA 3.60+ or $2,000 per year for GPA 3.0-3.59, renewable 3 more years (3.0 GPA, 12 credits a term). Students who finish the Undergraduate Foundation program with a 3.5 GPA get a $4,000 per year Year One Progression Award instead. A $2,000-per-semester International Merit Award is available after enrolling. The Common Data Set shows only non-need-based institutional aid for nonresidents.'
