update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs for 2026-27 from the Common Data Set (it lists the same rate for nonresident and international students; tuition varies by program for about 78% of undergraduates). The Common Data Set also shows 287 nonresidents received institutional aid, average $10,539 (total $3,024,685); No citizenship needed for admission or merit awards; all incoming students are considered automatically. Fall 2027 first-year awards: Warrior Award $6,500 per year, Gold Award $4,500 per year, Green Award up to $2,500 per year, each for four years (3.0 GPA and full-time enrollment to keep). Federal aid is for US citizens and permanent residents only. The Common Data Set shows both need-based and non-need-based institutional aid for nonresidents, but Wayne State''s pages describe only merit awards.'
