update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'First-year costs from the Common Data Set (private institution, one tuition for all; room only $12,845, food only $6,706). The Common Data Set says 2026-27 costs were not yet available, so these are most likely the 2025-26 figures. The Common Data Set marks the college''s own aid as ''need-based'': 158 nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid, average $9,677 (total $3,096,780). The international admissions page says a limited International Grant is available starting with fall 2026 applicants, and asks for proof of funds of USD $71,382; International students are considered for merit scholarships based on secondary-school results; the Presidential Merit Scholarship (tuition, renewable 8 semesters) averages $20,000-$25,000 for Wentworth students generally (page not specific to international students). Starting with fall 2026 applicants a limited number of need-based International Grants are offered; the need-based aid application must be filed before the admission decision. From the Common Data Set: 158 nonresidents received institutional aid, average $9,677.'
