update public.cost_aid t set notes = '2025-26 estimated annual cost for out-of-state undergraduates living on campus: tuition and fees $14,990, books $1,290, housing and meals $10,718, transportation $1,340, personal $2,390, loan fees $71, total $30,799. No separate international rate is printed (the international cost sheet linked from the admissions page is for 2021-22). The 2026-27 fee schedule PDF''s full-time row could not be read; College Navigator 2024-25: tuition includes required fees; total is the on-campus cost of attendance for West Virginia residents ($33,479 at the out-of-state rate); Yellow Jacket Scholarship table for out-of-state and international first-time freshmen by high school GPA (3.0-3.4 / 3.5-3.7 / 3.8-4.0): living on campus $3,000 / $4,500 / $6,000 per year; living off campus $2,000 / $3,000 / $4,000. The same page''s general eligibility says a FAFSA by June 30 for U.S. citizens and eligible noncitizens, so confirm with the university how international students qualify. Need-based aid for international students is not mentioned.'
