update public.cost_aid t set notes = 'YSU International Programs Office estimate for 2026-27 (9 months, 12-18 credits): average tuition and fees $17,177, room and board $12,000, books $1,200, mandatory health insurance $1,491; total $31,868. The tuition rate is locked for four years from first enrollment. International undergraduates pay the non-resident rate; First-year costs from the Common Data Set: it prints one nonresident tuition rate ($12,077) for out-of-state and international students. Only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; the recipient count and average were reported as N/A; International Scholarship Awards for first-time freshmen, by high school GPA: $1,000 (3.0-3.39), $2,000 (3.4-3.69), $3,000 (3.7+) per year, renewable up to 4 years with 24 credits per year and a 3.0 GPA; spring starters receive the award from the following fall. Sokolov Honors College (26 ACT/1240 SAT, 3.5 GPA): $1,000 tuition plus $2,000 housing. Federal aid is not available to international students.'
