update public.programs t set notes = 'Admission is to the Faculty of Science (Physical, Earth, Math & Computer Sciences group) and CS is then declared as a major. The admissions pages list ''typical minimum admission grades'' as guidelines only; they are not guaranteed offers, and McGill says the minimum varies from year to year. Fall 2027 entry: application deadline January 15, supporting documents March 1 (pages checked 2026-10-27). Fee: tuition line of the McGill 2026-27 international undergraduate table for the Bachelor of Science (CAD 64,785.90, rounded to 64,786); 2027-28 rates were not published, the table does not state the credit load, and it says tuition is guaranteed for the program length for students admitted in 2026-27. A-Level and IB ranges: https://www.mcgill.ca/undergraduate-admissions/apply/requirements/international/advanced-levels and https://www.mcgill.ca/undergraduate-admissions/apply/requirements/international/ib . AP / US route: https://www.mcgill.ca/undergraduate-admissions/apply/requirements/us (the US range there is shared by the Biological, Bio-Physical-Computational and Physical, Earth, Math and Computer Sciences groups). Fees: https://www.mcgill.ca/student-accounts/files/student-accounts/new_intl_ugrad_degree_students_admitted_2026-27_0.pdf . English: https://www.mcgill.ca/undergraduate-admissions/apply/english-proficiency . Course length is not stated on these pages, so none is shown.'
