  and t.slug = 'science-computing-and-software-systems'
  and i.id = t.institution_id
  and i.slug = 'melbourne';
update public.programs t set notes = 'Melbourne has no standalone economics bachelor''s degree: Economics is a major inside the Bachelor of Commerce (it is also a major in the Bachelor of Arts), so the entry requirements are those of the whole Bachelor of Commerce. The Entry score 2027 values are guide scores that match VCE-equivalent results; the domestic lowest selection rank for 2026 was 92. Fee not shown: Melbourne charges international fees per subject by discipline band, so the course page gives only a range for the whole Bachelor of Commerce, A$56,451 - A$62,464 for the first year in 2027 (total A$180,714 - A$200,139); the 2027 International Fee Tables list Accounting, Administration, Commerce and Economics subjects at A$61,312 per 100 credit points (1 EFTSL): https://study.unimelb.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0034/462949/2027-International-Fee-Tables.pdf. Direct applications for the 2027 start-year intake (Semester 1) close 30 November 2026 (international key dates: https://study.unimelb.edu.au/find/courses/undergraduate/bachelor-of-commerce/how-to-apply/). AP route: https://study.unimelb.edu.au/how-to-apply/undergraduate-study/recognised-vce-equivalent-qualifications/qualifications/united-states-high-school-diploma-and-satact . Major description: https://handbook.unimelb.edu.au/2026/components/b-com-major-4 .'
