update public.programs t set notes = 'Monash has a Bachelor of Economics (B2031) with its own entry scores, listed here instead of Commerce. 2027 intake entry scores from the course page''s international view; the ATAR of 87.5 is the Australian Year 12 score. Fee is the 2027 international fee for 48 credit points (a standard full-time year). Starts in February, July or November; Monash publishes no closing date for international applicants outside Year 12 (apply any time of year; https://www.monash.edu/admissions/apply/international-ug). Clayton only; the four specialisations are Business analytics for economics, Economics and economic policy, Macroeconomics and financial markets, and Mathematical economics and econometrics. The VCE prerequisites are not shown. For qualifications other than IB or Australian Year 12, Monash assumes the equivalent maths knowledge if you completed maths at the required level (no AP course is named), so confirm with Monash.'
