update public.programs t set notes = 'Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences, Department of Economics; both a BA and a BSc in Economics exist and the program page says you can start at the Burnaby or Surrey campus. The page does not state the degree length, so the course length is not shown. Fee: 2026/27 international tuition is $1,262.88 per unit for students who entered 2024/25 or later; $37,886 = 30 units a year at that rate (the SFU typical-costs page gives $18,943.20 tuition per 15-unit term) from https://www.sfu.ca/students/calendar/2026/fall/fees-and-regulations/tuition-fees/undergraduate.html and https://www.sfu.ca/students/financial-aid/plan/typical-costs.html ; 2027/28 fees are not yet published and SFU says international fees may rise by up to 6% a year. Deadline: Fall 2027 applications open 1 Oct 2026, deadline 31 Jan 2027, all admission documents due 28 Feb 2027 (https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/apply/dates-deadlines/high-school/fall-term.html). Requirements: US https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/usa-highschool.html ; UK https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/international-highschool/country/united-kingdom.html ; IB https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/international-baccalaureate.html ; AP https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/advanced-placement.html ; grade ranges https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/historical-admission-grade-ranges.html (guide only, no guarantee).'
