update public.programs t set notes = 'Faculty of Applied Sciences, School of Engineering Science: mandatory co-op, and students specialize in one of five options by third year (Biomedical, Computer, Electronics, Engineering Physics, Systems). Mechatronic Systems Engineering is a separate SFU program with the same course requirements and was not chosen because Engineering Science is the broader entry. The program page does not state the degree length or campus, so the course length is not shown. Fee: 2026/27 international tuition is $1,262.88 per unit for students who entered 2024/25 or later; $37,886 = 30 units a year at that rate (the SFU typical-costs page gives $18,943.20 tuition per 15-unit term); 200/300/400 division courses in Engineering Science cost more ($1,348.19 per unit) and co-op terms are $932.08 per term (https://www.sfu.ca/students/calendar/2026/fall/fees-and-regulations/tuition-fees/undergraduate.html , https://www.sfu.ca/students/financial-aid/plan/typical-costs.html). 2027/28 fees are not yet published and SFU says international fees may rise by up to 6% a year. Deadline: Fall 2027 applications open 1 Oct 2026, deadline 31 Jan 2027, all admission documents due 28 Feb 2027 (https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/apply/dates-deadlines/high-school/fall-term.html). Requirements: US https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/usa-highschool.html ; UK https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/international-highschool/country/united-kingdom.html ; IB https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/international-baccalaureate.html ; AP https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/advanced-placement.html ; grade ranges https://www.sfu.ca/students/admission/admission-requirements/historical-admission-grade-ranges.html (guide only, no guarantee).'
