update public.programs t set notes = '2027 entry, Semester 1 (February) and Semester 2 (August) intakes. The Bachelor of Advanced Computing is Sydney''s main computing degree (Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Software Development or Computational Data Science specialisations); the BSc with a Computer Science major is not covered here. Entry values come from the course page set to ''International student, 2027'': entry score 90.0 ATAR (indicative, a guide and subject to change), fee A$63,600 (page says estimate only, year 1 of 48 credit points). The qualification scores (IB 34, GCE 15/16, AP 13/16/3.2, SAT 1340, ACT 28) are the page''s ''Find your qualification'' data. The deadline is the general international undergraduate closing date for Semester 1: 1 December 2026 (page https://www.sydney.edu.au/study/applying/application-dates.html, which says to check the course page and apply early). Apply directly or through an authorised agent; UAC is mandatory only for current Australian Year 12 students or IB students in Australia. AP route: same course page.'
