update public.programs t set notes = 'Economics (Major, Minor, Specialist) is admitted through the Social Sciences category (OUAC code TAX) at St. George; no supplementary application. Fall 2027 entry (the pages say ''2027 admissions''). U of T publishes no A Level grade or IB point offer for this category. The program page lists English plus Calculus & Vectors (MCV4U) as the prerequisites for the Ontario system; the curriculum-specific equivalents are on https://future.utoronto.ca/requirements-international-high-schools and in the 2027-28 International Undergraduate Admissions Bulletin https://internationalprograms.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/2027-28-International-UAB.pdf. Deadlines: https://future.utoronto.ca/deadlines (apply by 15 Jan 2027, recommended early date 7 Nov 2026, documents 1 Feb 2027). Fee: the international fee, CAD 66110, is the 2026-27 approved first-year international tuition for Arts & Science; incidental/ancillary fees and health insurance are extra. This is a 2026-27 value, not Fall 2027; the planned 2027-28 figure is 68750 (information only, subject to change). Fee source: https://planningandbudget.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026-27-Tuition-Fee-Report_FINAL.pdf (Tuition Fee Schedules for Publicly-Funded Programs 2026-27, Table D1).'
