update public.programs t set notes = 'Admission category: Computer Science (OUAC code TAD), St. George, Faculty of Arts & Science. Fall 2027 entry (the pages say ''2027 admissions''). U of T publishes no A Level grade or IB point offer for this category; admission is competitive and based on the overall academic record and the supplementary application (people with any post-secondary study cannot apply directly into Computer Science). Requirements by curriculum: https://future.utoronto.ca/requirements-international-high-schools and the 2027-28 International Undergraduate Admissions Bulletin https://internationalprograms.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/2027-28-International-UAB.pdf. Deadlines: https://future.utoronto.ca/deadlines (apply by 15 Jan 2027, recommended early date 7 Nov 2026, documents 1 Feb 2027, Computer Science supplementary application 1 Feb 2027). Fee: the international fee, CAD 66110, is the 2026-27 approved first-year international tuition for Arts & Science (Computer Science students pay the general Arts & Science fee in year 1 and a higher fee from year 2: 69030 in 2026-27); incidental/ancillary fees and health insurance are extra. This is a 2026-27 value, not Fall 2027; the planned 2027-28 first-year Arts & Science figure is 68750 (information only, subject to change; the upper-year Computer Science fee is planned at 72480). Fee source: https://planningandbudget.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026-27-Tuition-Fee-Report_FINAL.pdf (Tuition Fee Schedules for Publicly-Funded Programs 2026-27, Tables D1 and D2).'
