update public.programs t set notes = 'Fall 2027 entry (the Engineering page uses a September 2027 start in its examples). Engineering admits directly to Mechanical Engineering. Prerequisite courses must be completed within five years of the start date. Offers per curriculum from the Engineering out-of-country page https://discover.engineering.utoronto.ca/how-to-apply/outofcanada/ (A Level and IB entries are minimums for consideration, not offer grades; the page says most programs require higher). Deadlines: https://future.utoronto.ca/deadlines (apply 15 Jan 2027, recommended early date 7 Nov 2026, Engineering documents and ESA 15 Jan 2027). Fee: the international fee, CAD 72860, is the 2026-27 approved international tuition for Applied Science & Engineering (first-year guide: https://firstyear.engineering.utoronto.ca/finances/); incidental fees and health insurance are extra. This is a 2026-27 value, not Fall 2027; the planned 2027-28 figure is 75770 (information only, subject to change). Fee source: https://planningandbudget.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2026-27-Tuition-Fee-Report_FINAL.pdf (Tuition Fee Schedules for Publicly-Funded Programs 2026-27, Table D1).'
