update public.programs t set notes = '2027 entry (Semester 1 starts 22 Feb 2027). The guide score shown is the lowest adjusted ATAR/Rank UQ made an offer to in Semester 1 2026 (UQ updates these guide scores each April; meeting it does not guarantee admission). The international score table (A-level, IB, AP, SAT, ACT) is the page''s own ''minimum entry score'' tool for a student who studied in the United States (data from https://study.uq.edu.au/api/program-requirements/2467-2027?year=2027&country=United%20States&term=7720); the same A-level and IB scores appear for England. Fee is the page''s ''Approximate yearly cost of tuition (16 units)'' for international students, 2027 (AUD). Applications direct to UQ (or via a UQ agent) for Semester 1 close 30 November of the previous year, i.e. 30 Nov 2026; students whose senior schooling is Australian Year 12 or IB in Australia apply via QTAC instead. The domestic table on the same page shows ATAR 82 / IB 31, while the international qualification table returns IB 32 for this program; the IB points shown follow the international table. CRICOS 001948F.'
